INSERT INTO missionObjectives (missionID, briefingText) VALUES
(55184,'I want these elite troops delivered to for inspection. We hired them recently from an Amarrian security firm to work as guards on our transport vessels. Standard procedure requires that they be inspected for any possible diseases or mental disorders before they''re allowed on board.'),
(55186,'"The deal," as you so quaintly put it, my young friend, is this: The station manager of recently reported to us a serious lack of mono-cell batteries in their supply depot, a situation that could result in a temporary shutdown of the entire station. We need to help them out, and I''d like you to deliver the necessary goods to them. Simple enough, eh? Well, are you interested or not? I know of several others who would happily take this offer in your stead.'),
(55187,'We were ordered by high ranking officials in the to deliver a batch of Zemnar to the inhabitants of . Their supplies are low and they need some backup incase of a viral outbreak. |collapsed= yes'),
(55188,'I have just the thing you want. A relative of mine in just requested a special order of genetically enhanced livestock. I''d like you to deliver them to him in person; he''ll meet you on . And keep a lid on this, will you? Some consumers, especially religious Amarrians, would boycott his wares if word got out he uses genetically enhanced animals.'),
(55189,'Yes, I have something for you. A group of lads from have been requested by the army to . I''ve agreed to their request, and I''d like you to carry it out. Deliver them to their destination, the faster the better.'),
(55191,'Yes, I have something for you. One of our transports flying through broke down and requires immediate repairs. We''ve agreed to send him the spare parts he needs to complete the operation, and I''d like you to deliver the goods. If you''re fast he might even make it on time, so don''t tarry!'),
(55192,'I have just the thing you want. To eliminate the depressive mood of our hangar staff, cargo bay workers, janitors and other laborers we decided to throw them a party at . I''d like you to do the honors of delivering the spiced wine to the gathering. And don''t forget, a quick delivery will get you a bonus!'),
(55193,'I have just the thing you want. A spate of engine failures and system crashes at a client firm in has forced them to come to us for more coolants. We have some extras available, which I''d like you to deliver. Get it done in time, before their manager suffers a nervous breakdown, to earn your bonus.'),
(55194,'Yes, I have something for you. The local news recently aired a story on poor immigrants in . Apparently some of the families have fallen on hard times and lack the funds to even buy the most basic necessities. A few concerned citizens in asked me to have these clothes delivered to the needy in , which they can make use of. I''d like you to make the first leg of the trip, which is to drop off the goods at . Officials at the station will take care of the rest.'),
(55208,'Yes, I have something for you. The greenhouses at need a delivery of fertile soil. Take these crates and deliver them, would you? Thanks. Have an excellent day!'),
(56871,'Damnation, they''re sending them out younger and younger. Are you sure you''re old enough to fly a starship? Oh, well, we have to play the hand we''re dealt, and if you''re the best I can get, I suppose you''ll do. We''ll start simple, youngster. Banidine is normally all but worthless, so real miners don''t usually bother with the stuff. Still, I''ve found a buyer who''s willing to take whatever we can mine. So, get me 20,000 units of Banidine and I''ll make it worth your while. It should be easy, even for a pup like you, but it will show me that you''re serious. There''s an asteroid field near here that''s lousy with the stuff – I''ve bookmarked it for you. Get back as soon as you can and I''ll arrange a little bonus.'),
(56875,'We''ve found a conglomeration of Augumene asteroids nearby. The ore''s not much good to anyone due to the exorbitant cost of reprocessing, of course, but a couple of our scientists are interested in doing some research on such a rare substance. In any case, hopefully you''ve been around the block enough times that you can find the ore and bring it in.'),
(56878,'Oh, right. I was thinking I''d already sent you a com-chat about this. Heh. Sorry. One of our sources obtained information on the whereabouts of a significant deposit of Mercium ore. It would be disastrous for our cause if this Mercium were to fall into Amarrian or Caldari hands. Unfortunately, we''re certain that they already know about it, so as I said, we must work quickly. Remember, they want that Mercium, so that means we need it more. Get it? You do whatever you have to to get this done quickly, alright?'),
(56879,'Oh, right. I was thinking I''d already sent you a com-chat about this. Heh. Sorry. One of our sources obtained information on the whereabouts of a significant deposit of Mercium ore. It would be disastrous for our cause if this Mercium were to fall into Amarrian or Caldari hands. Unfortunately, we''re certain that they already know about it, so as I said, we must work quickly. Remember, they want that Mercium, so that means we need it more. Get it? You do whatever you have to to get this done quickly, alright?'),
(56880,'Oh, right. I was thinking I''d already sent you a com-chat about this. Heh. Sorry. One of our sources obtained information on the whereabouts of a significant deposit of Mercium ore. It would be disastrous for our cause if this Mercium were to fall into Amarrian or Caldari hands. Unfortunately, we''re certain that they already know about it, so as I said, we must work quickly. Remember, they want that Mercium, so that means we need it more. Get it? You do whatever you have to to get this done quickly, alright?'),
(56881,'Well, we''ve got a bit of a weird one here. We''ve found an old mining post in . But, the thing is, we can''t find who used to own it: There are no records of its being built or even existing. It''s simply empty. No sign of anyone left there, dead or otherwise. Our initial investigation found extensive fire damage, gas leaks — you name it, it went wrong. Lots of explosive damage, though we can''t tell if that was accidental or intentional. And some marks... well, we just don''t know what could do that to metal. It''s damn creepy, that''s for sure. Anyway, near as we can tell, the miners were working on a large Lyavite deposit. They didn''t finish, because there''s still about 5,000 units of it at the site. Now, I know Lyavite isn''t the most popular rock, but nobody just leaves that much ore lying around. And besides, the brains at the lab figure they can use the stuff for some of their research, so this opportunity is too good to pass up. That''s where you come in. Warp in, mine the Lyavite, and warp out. It''s that easy.'),
(56901,'Excellent. As you know, it is the duty of every citizen to demonstrate his or her loyalty to the state from time to time. Though you are, at present, a small cog in the great machine of the Empire, you will find that even you have your place. We have a task for you that will help show your fitness to advance in our society and become a more significant part of that great machine. It seems that the construction works at are experiencing an unfortunate labor shortage, possibly brought on by their overly harsh personnel management methods. It is important to the Empire that we get them a shipment of elite slaves so that they do not fall any further behind schedule. Are you a loyal enough citizen to do this task and do it quickly? I will upload a bookmark to your People & Places databank; use it to locate and reach your destination.'),
(56903,'Well, yes. Now, I can''t say too much, but something''s come up, and there''s a great need for ground troops in a nearby system. You may have noticed all those marines hanging out in the loading bay. We''ve grabbed every available transport we can find, but there''s still a few left behind who need to be transported to . Suffice to say, their presence is of vital importance to Federation efforts, and if you''re a loyal citizen, you''ll take them to their destination. And of course there''s some extra pay in it for you. Will you help? |collapsed= yes'),
(56913,'Yes, I think you are. Listen, our miners have just reported a bunch of rogue drones in the system. Between them and the damned ore thieves, I''m almost ready to give up. They''re worse than Gallentean greenroaches – if we don''t show them that they''re not welcome here, we''ll be up to our eyeballs. And I can''t send my guys out there if I know they might be in danger. No, we need a capsuleer on this job, someone capable of defending a ship and mining at the same time. I''ve bookmarked a mining site for you. Go on out there and, if you see any drones, take ''em out. Be caref— well, I don''t need to tell an experienced starship captain like you. You know the risks. Then mine whatever Banidine you find out there so I can find out what the damn things are so interested in.'),
(56915,'A recent survey scan of reveals a big deposit of Banidine ore. We were content to leave it alone at first, but then we saw swarms of drones in the area. They seem to be making their way through the asteroid fields there in a hurry. They haven''t stumbled on the Banidine yet, but it''s only a matter of time. We want you to get to the ore before they do. I won''t lie to you; it''s going to be close. You may even have to fight a few of them off, so be careful.'),
(56916,'wants a massive shipment of Augumene right away, so we need you to get out there and bring some back. They seem to think they might be able to find some use for the stuff for chemical warfare, I guess? But that''s just between you and me, right? Anyway, I''ve been looking for a miner who''s experienced enough, with the right kind of ship, and maybe you fit the bill. Time is critical on this one. There''s a big bonus for you if you can bring it in fast enough. Seriously, we need a mountain of this stuff, so get on it. I''ve uploaded the location to your People & Places databank.'),
(56919,'You ever try mining with drones? Useful little guys, huh? Yeah, well, to a point… Turns out someone got the bright idea that if mining drones mine more ore, bigger drones would mine even more ore. This guy''s team slapped some mining drone''s AI into non-regulation heavy combat units and threw some mining lasers on. He even hacked the firmware so that the mining brains could control the weaponry, making some sort of self-sufficient mining machines. But of course the genius didn''t test the things properly before sending them out to to mine Mercium. And of course now he''s made himself scarce. You can probably guess what happened. Now there''s a bunch of haywire drones zipping about this rare mineral that we want — our guys in the lab need it for research, I guess. The drones aren''t even mining the rock, last I heard, but they have tried to bore through any ship we send out there.... It''s getting ridiculous. If you can, get out to , neutralize the drones, and bring back all the Mercium; we''ll pay you well for your efforts.'),
(56920,'I''ve just discovered a sizable deposit of Pithix out by an old mining station. The station''s been abandoned for a while now, but there are still working sensors in the area; that''s how we picked up on the Pithix. Problem is, the transmission''s hardly secure. I need you to get out there and bring me back that rock before someone else cleans the place out. So, are you game?'),
(56923,'Right away. But look, this one''s a little weird. Just a heads up. There''s this guy who''s making these really, truly gigantic ice sculptures — some kinda artsy shit, I don''t know. I said, buddy, that much ice, it''s gonna melt before you can finish carving it, or it''s gonna break under its own weight. He says he knows that, says that''s why he''s gonna build it in space! Crazy… Anyway, he''s got the money, so what am I gonna say but "how much and how fast?" So, can you get 20 units of Crystalline Icicles over here ASAP? I got a location for you. {{Co|red|You will need an Ice Harvester module to complete this mission. Also, be aware that this amount of raw Crystalline Icicles ore may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space'),
(56924,'Alright! You ever been out to some of those backwater colonies? You know the ones I mean. Barren wastelands of rocks and dust where some nut got the bright idea to try to build the agricultural community of tomorrow? Kind of place where the main export is despair? That kind of place? Well, so happens I know of one that''s just starting up. Poor bastards need some fuel. They''re willing to pay good money, too. Now, I could sell them the good stuff, but seriously, these jokers wouldn''t know good ice if it fell out of the sky and crushed their pet furrier. There''s a field of Azure Ice at Hageken. It''s not as good as Blue Ice, but the colonists won''t know the difference. Bring me back about, oh, 20 blocks of it. I''ll sell it to the colony goobers and cut you in. Sound good? You will need an Ice Harvester module to complete this mission. Also, be aware that this amount of raw Azure Ice may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space.'),
(56927,'Well, we''ve located some asteroids that contain substantial amounts of Polygypsum. It''s a comparatively rare mineral, and almost completely unknown in this system. Our guys want to have a look at the stuff and see if they can figure out some way to make use of it; however, we don''t have anyone who wants to deal with the stuff. So guess who I thought of first? You''ll need to grab all 2,800 units of the stuff and get it back here. So what do you think? Are you in?'),
(56928,'has an unusual request for the right miner. We need a big shipment of Geodite crystals for a client of ours, some gemology lab. Maybe you''ve heard of Geodite, but if not, it''d be no surprise — the stuff''s pretty much worthless. But these gemologists figure they might be able to get some decent stones out of it and make a bit of profit that way. Whatever. They want to pay for it, so it''s all good by me. And you''ll get your cut, don''t worry. Anyway, if you''re interested, I''ll send the coordinates over to your ship''s NeoCom — the field''s in this system.'),
(56929,'It''s the sound of war! It''s been too long since the blaring of military marches has been heard, the stockpiling of weapons undertaken, the murderous idealism of a young generation inveigled. And to me it all seems like the clinking of ISK. War is one of the biggest boons to business you could hope for. It''s a hungry giant that will eat anything you can throw at it. And the thing is, if you don''t feed it, it will just eat you…. But if you feed it well? Oh, the rewards. Public recognition, sure, but the contracts, the contracts, ! That''s where the real ISK is. And we''re going to get those contracts. Oh, yes. But first we need minerals. Right now, it seems the giant on our doorstep wants Oeryl, and we''re going to give it to him. There''s a deposit out at . Bring back all 5,600 units of the stuff and I''ll make sure you get your share of the reward.'),
(56934,'The government says we''re prepared for war. You wouldn''t know it by looking at our wounded. Space makes everything worse. Just look through the medical bay. Second-degree burns and frostbite are both alarmingly common, and are usually in conjunction with other serious injuries. I need pain medications badly. I can''t just wait for the next delivery. I need to produce my own drugs. For that I''m going to need Gamboge Cytoserocin. I heard a smuggler say there was a pocket at . Go there, and bring back everything you can. I''ll try to make it worth your while. {{Co|red|You must own and be able to use a Gas Cloud Harvester to complete this mission. If you do not or cannot, please just decline; note that you can decline one mission every 4 hours without standing loss.'),
(57114,'Well, you''re pretty green, by the look of you, but I''ve got no choice. You may have heard all the rumors. The entire frontier is buzzing with reports that we''re pretty much at war with the Amarrians. I can''t say either way, for sure, but I do know that all this war talk has led to some big headaches when it comes to commercial traffic and trade-route management. Passenger liners are all booked, haulers have been pre-empted by the military or by wealthy clients... god, it''s just a mess out there. Anyway, as you may have seen, the docks here at are filled to overflowing with tons of goods, and we can''t seem to find enough transport to get them to their destinations. I need to get some of this stuff out of here. Ah, here: we''ve got a shipment of vaccines that need to be delivered to in a hurry. I''m willing to provide a substantial bonus if they''re delivered right away. Regardless, the meds need to be delivered soon, though. Say the word and you can move the stuff into your cargo hold. Can you do it?'),
(57174,'I''ve been having a spot of bother filling an order, . It''s starting to affect my usually sunny disposition. I''m hoping you can clear this off my docket, and bring the smile back to my face. My client requires hydrogen isotopes to run her control tower, and she''s getting a little snippy about the time it''s taking me to provide it. She''s even sent along a few assassins to vent her displeasure. No patience, that woman. , I need you to procure 10 units of a very particular ice-- Azure Ice, I believe, is what you''re looking for on your scanner; I can extract the hydrogen myself. I''ve lost a few good ships and a few incompetent pilots in the ice fields trying to fill this order, and I really need you to live up to your reputation, -- within the next 24 hours. Can I count on you, ?'),
(57288,'We recently found a number of new mining fields in adjacent systems, and the usual assortment of pirate trash has come out of the woodwork to exploit it. We''ll need them mined soon because even those thieving bastards have friends in places high enough to put the legal status of these sites in doubt. For some reason they''ve taken an interest even in Banidine, too, and we''ll need to find out why; all my workers are busy with the more profitable fields, but I''m not taking any chances. I''m uploading a bookmark to your People & Places databank; it shows the location of a Banidine mining operation. I need you to head out there and mine all the Banidine — should be 18,000 units, my foreman tells me. Once we''ve made an undisputed claim, we''re free to mine there again without interference, and I''ll provide you with a little something for your trouble.'),
(57826,'Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. Looks like there was some kind of explosion on a colony in this system, and thousands of people are without a home. I want you to take some of them over to so we can do our part in providing shelter for less fortunate people.'),
(57832,'Sure, I''ve got something. is in the middle of constructing an outpost in . Our engineers there claim to lack a few loads of construction blocks to finish the work, and I was asked to deliver some blocks to that station. Could you please take the material straight to ? Our people in will take care of retrieving them from your hangar there for the construction project.'),
(57833,'For you, my friend, there''s always something. One commodity we all have a hard time living without is oxygen. One of our buyers is on a station that''s close to running out of air, so I want you to fly over to and give them a bit more.'),
(57834,'An arms dealer passing through the system just sold us a cache of weapons. I need you to take it to for me. Don''t worry, we''ve already acquired a permit for them, so you won''t have any trouble at customs.'),
(57835,'Yes, I have something for you. It''s tough to quit smoking when you''ve got a warehouse full of cigarettes within arm''s reach. Take every crate of that crap you can find in that warehouse over to and leave it there. Quickly, before I change my mind!'),
(57838,'Sure, I''ve got something. I have assets at that are in need of additional protection. We''ve hired a group of marines to take care of the problem. Go to and drop them off.'),
(57847,'Yes, I have something for you. One of our transports flying through broke down and requires immediate repairs. We''ve agreed to send him the spare parts he needs to complete the operation, and I''d like you to deliver the goods. If you''re fast he might even make it on time, so don''t tarry!'),
(57850,'For you, my friend, there''s always something. A few colleagues of mine are on an assignment in and requested a batch of transmitters which they need for a particular task. I need them delivered there A.S.A.P. You''re up for the job, I presume?'),
(57851,'Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. I''ve been ordered by the government to have these fertilizers delivered to , from where they''ll be dispersed to nearby bio-domes. Quite a mundane job but one that needs to be done. Obviously I''d like you to do the honors of making the delivery, so here you go.'),
(57855,'Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. Looks like there was some kind of explosion on a colony in this system, and thousands of people are without a home. I want you to take some of them over to so we can do our part in providing shelter for less fortunate people.'),
(57856,'I have just the thing you want. Bio-engineers and farmers in nearby settlements, which have been supplying us with foodstuffs, have had good fortune recently. Their supplies of frozen plant seeds are overflowing, and they would like to sell some of their excess products. Obviously we took advantage of a good opportunity and bought the goods for silly prices, those people are so gullible. I''d like you to deliver the goods to , where we''ve found a buyer.'),
(57871,'Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. Miners stopping by for supplies is a common occurrence. It so happens that a few of them left off in a hurry, and forgot a load of drill parts in the cargo bay. Fortunately for them the containers were marked, which allowed us to trace the owners quickly enough. When we contacted them they requested we send the parts to , for a fee of course. If you''ll do the honors of transporting the goods, a part of that fee will be yours.'),
(57873,'I have just the thing you want. We''ve decided to do our agents in a favor. They''ve been complaining for quite some time of being overworked and underpaid, so we''ve decided to send them the perfect gift to soothe their nerves. A few packs of tobacco should do the trick, heh heh. It''s at least something, until we come up with a better solution. Deliver the batch to and a local supplier will pick it up from there and deliver it to where they''re staying.'),
(57878,'Sure, I''ve got something. is in the middle of constructing an outpost in . Our engineers there claim to lack a few loads of construction blocks to finish the work, and I was asked to deliver some blocks to that station. Could you please take the material straight to ? Our people in will take care of retrieving them from your hangar there for the construction project.'),
(57880,'For you, my friend, there''s always something. A few colleagues of mine are on an assignment in and requested a batch of transmitters which they need for a particular task. I need them delivered there A.S.A.P. You''re up for the job, I presume?'),
(57881,'Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. I''ve been ordered by the government to have these fertilizers delivered to , from where they''ll be dispersed to nearby bio-domes. Quite a mundane job but one that needs to be done. Obviously I''d like you to do the honors of making the delivery, so here you go.'),
