 to the project, but with potentially many hundreds of billions of ISK riding on the successful integration of Ditanium into our armor plates and other protective ship components, we are taking no chances. We need to know immediately if you will deliver this Ditanium to the designated station.'),
(58553,'Oh, right. I was thinking I''d already sent you a com-chat about this. Heh. Sorry. One of our sources obtained information on the whereabouts of a significant deposit of Mercium ore. It would be disastrous for our cause if this Mercium were to fall into Amarrian or Caldari hands. Unfortunately, we''re certain that they already know about it, so as I said, we must work quickly. Remember, they want that Mercium, so that means we need it more. Get it? You do whatever you have to to get this done quickly, alright?'),
(60000,'We have a planetary situation we need your help with. A group of pro-Amarr terrorists is wreaking havoc in outlying provinces, and the local government''s hired a group of mercenaries to deal with them. You know mercs, I''m sure; they never really listen to anyone they think is softer than they are. We''re having trouble finding an ordinary captain who''s willing to ferry the guys over to for transit planetside. I think they''ll be more likely to behave if the captain is someone who can and will follow through on a threat to vent the ship to vacuum. Someone like you, in other words. Can we count on you to keep the unruly lot in line?'),
(60001,'One of my clients asked me to send over drones to replace the ones his company''s been losing in the line of work. That''s all he said. He never said anything about needing mining drones; of course I sent him a set of scout drones, and he was very upset at me for not being able to read his mind. People should be more specific about things. Take these mining drones over to for him, and if he asks why the paint looks new, tell him they''re fresh off the production line.'),
(60002,'Let me start at the beginning. As you have probably seen on the news channels, a prominent Caldari mining company is in the middle of a very nasty battle for economic survival with a new, up-and-coming mining company from within the same large conglomerate. Both of these companies specialize in the extraction of ores from some of the more inhospitable and dangerous locations in this and several adjoining systems. While this can be hazardous with regard to men and equipment, the profit potential from these largely untapped ore reserves can be quite significant, which brings me to our current predicament. As you may know, the specialized manual labor required for some of these mines can be significant in terms of numbers. Well, the Mining Health and Safety Commission, or MHSC, for this region recently conducted a survey of the first company''s operations, and found that their mining practices at certain locations may have resulted in excessive pollution, then further alleged a corresponding link to long-term miner health problems. The company has loudly complained that this is a ridiculous witch hunt brought about by their new competitor, which happens to have several “friends” on the commission. While they work to ensure they are equally “represented” on that commission, the recent finding has mandated that they immediately improve worker conditions and reduce pollution or risk losing their mining rights. To remedy this problem, they recently purchased a large number of the latest environmentally-friendly – and obscenely expensive – manportable drills, which seems to have assuaged the MHSC for the moment. They do, however, have a deadline for actually putting these new drills into the hands of the miners, which brings us to the reason I contacted you. We need you to deliver a rather large shipment of drills and other related equipment to a station that serves as a central service hub. From there, logistics pilots will deliver this and other items to the various mines in the system. Will you take on this important job?'),
(60003,'I like nice things, . Who doesn''t? Handing missions out to you people all day doesn''t offer nearly enough to cover my expenses, so a friend and I run a shipping business out to Syndicate space. Nothing big enough to interfere with the Syndicate itself, mind you. We provide a humanitarian service importing the latest holos from the heart of civilization. It''s the only way they can get the things for a reasonable cost – buying them direct from the companies in the Federation incurs immense shipping charges. Our usual courier is out of commission today, with her ship in for repairs after a pirate attack. If you want to make yourself useful, take the latest shipment over to and ask for Amelyn. They''ll know who you mean, just say that “Imba” sent you.'),
(60004,'As you almost certainly know, many decades ago our Grand Fleet met the hated Jovians on the field of battle in a system known as Vak-Atioth. Most unfortunately, our fleet was destroyed by the technologically superior Jovian ships and their advanced weaponry, marking one of the darkest moments in our history. Still, we learned much from this encounter, and the lessons learned there continue to benefit our military to this day, which brings us to why I called you here. Several days ago, Imperial naval intelligence mounted a highly classified effort to revisit the Vak-Atioth system, now known simply as Atioth, to conduct a final intensive search for any remaining debris that might provide some insight into the tactics and weapons used by the Jovians. Needless to say, this once-massive floating graveyard has long since been picked over by not only our own salvage fleets, but by scavengers and opportunists alike. All has not been lost, however. Much to our surprise, the Anathema covert ops ships sent to scan this system returned with a damaged but still readable supply of TIL-1A Nexus Chips. A preliminary review of the information they contain reveals only a portion of the great battle. We are hoping, however, that a more thorough analysis of these chips will reveal some insight into Jovian tactics and technology. If nothing else, they provide a very rare first-hand accounting of the battle which will add greatly to our historical archives and, when displayed at one of our leading military academies, will provide a stirring motivational icon for future generations of brave Imperial naval warriors. Now that you understand the importance of these chips to the Empire, I must ask: will you transport this invaluable cargo to the designated station?'),
(60005,'I have a very special mission for you today, . A high-ranked Overseer of a secret compound in has requested items of ours that must be delivered to him A.S.A.P. This job must be done in complete secrecy; we do not want the contents of this delivery to fall into the wrong hands. As a precautionary measure, we have set up an explosive mechanism inside the cargo containers that will trigger should anyone attempt to tamper with them. I trust you on this, . Be very discreet and, at any cost, avoid confrontation with hostiles en route to your destination. Make haste!'),
(60006,'I hope I can trust you to be discreet, . As part of a goodwill gesture to the Nefantar tribe, the Republic has offered allotments of planetary territory within our space on which to build embassies or summer homes or whatever else they need land for. I don''t care what it is, I don''t trust ‘em, but the government is determined to make sure we all get along. Yesterday I got an alert from one of my colleagues; it seems one Nefantar house is in collusion with elements from the Empire. Obviously we can''t just point fingers without evidence, but I''m in a perfect position to obtain that. The contractor they hired to design and build a house on their new property is a friend of mine. He''s given us one shipment of interior facing materials to seed with nanite spyware. Take the load to the depot at ; I know I can trust you to keep quiet about the additions to the cargo.'),
(60007,'We have several research outposts in various w-space systems. It''s one of those things that nobody discusses but everybody knows about anyway. They''ve recovered bits of ancient technology which seem to have unusual properties... well, compared to what we''re used to seeing, at least. We''re hoping these might be a clue to the Sleepers'' technology... but it could easily be remnants of a scrapyard, for all we know. Take these samples over to the lab at , so we can figure out what we''ve got.'),
(60008,'As you know, Amarr warships rely heavily on the various armors that we use in the construction and upgrading of our ships. For the most part, we rely on the same metals and alloys found in markets and hangars found in virtually every corner of the populated regions. Thus, it is a rare thing when a wholly new metal appears – and rarer still when only one race discovers it, unbeknownst to the others. Such an occurrence, I can tell you now only in the strictest confidence, has indeed taken place at a remote clandestine Amarr metallurgical research facility. Masquerading as a routine ore processing laboratory near an otherwise uninteresting Veldspar-laden asteroid field, this facility has been conducting advanced research exclusively into an extremely rare and highly classified metal, found only in the ore of a small fraction of the asteroids present in that specific field: a new metal we call Ditanium. To date, this is the strongest naturally occurring metal yet encountered by our scientists. While we are confident that this metal exists elsewhere in space, to our knowledge, we are the first to actually find it. Given the rarity of this metal and the significant complexities of its mining and processing, it has taken two full months to produce just enough finished metal plates to fit a single Punisher-class frigate. We intend to use this ship for Phase I field testing, which includes flight handling characteristics, radar cross-section analysis, temperature extremes testing, and other critical operational parameters. If successful, we are confident that we may be able to begin full scale production and ship fitting within two years. However, before this test can take place, we need someone to courier these Ditanium plates to a station we designate. From there, it will be transshipped to a military shipyard for fitting to the Punisher testbed ship. We do not anticipate this shipment will present any problems, particularly given the high level of secrecy relating to the project, but with potentially many hundreds of billions of ISK riding on the successful integration of Ditanium into our armor plates and other protective ship components, we are taking no chances. We need to know immediately if you will deliver this Ditanium to the designated station.'),
(60009,'As you know, there are many hundreds of thousands of Minmatar slaves working to provide essential services to the Empire, just as they have for centuries. Given their considerable natural physical abilities, they have always made up one of the most important and valuable ethnic groups within the vast Amarr slave workforce. One unavoidable consequence of this, however, is that we have had to invest a considerable amount of money, not only in the health and welfare of these slaves, but also to ensure their obedience. One important aspect of this latter effort has been the establishment of Labor Reeducation Centers, or LRC''s, which are designed to house some of the more problematic slaves in order to facilitate their eventual return to the workforce. In recent months, however, there has been a significant increase in violent disobedience at certain LRC''s, with some of the more severe instances leading to near-riots. Our immediate problem is that one of these facilities, , has been taken over during just such an uprising. The slaves have reportedly killed and injured dozens of our personnel and taken the remainder hostage. They are demanding the immediate release of their fellow slaves at a nearby Amarr mining operation, along with transportation to a destination of their choosing. We have, so far, managed to keep this incident quiet; if the Minmatar Republic leadership were to learn of this, it could very easily lead to much more severe consequences for both races. The only way to ensure this does not happen is through the immediate application of overwhelming force. Therefore, we need you to deliver a large contingent of specially trained Riot Interdiction Teams to a nearby station, from which they will join up with other security elements for final transportation to . Will you assist us? |collapsed= yes'),
(60010,'I''m not going to beat around the bush with you on this one, as there isn''t any time. We have a developing emergency in <System.. Several of our commercial convoys have been ripped to shreds in the last few months by an extremely dangerous band of terrorists. As you can see from these camera drone recordings, they have even been willing to fly their ships directly into our freighters and other unarmed haulers. And yes, before you ask, we have been escorting these convoys with heavily armed security vessels, though to little effect. As these terrorists are obviously willing to die for their cause, they aren''t bothering to attack our warships. They simply seem to appear out of nowhere, accelerate to high speeds and slam into the cargo ships. Depending on the cargo, this action can, at best, tear open the cargo bays and release the contents into the vacuum of space, or, at worst, strike a shipment of fuels or ammunition, and destroy the freighter in one huge explosion. One such explosion destroyed an entire convoy. However, an ultra-secure communications intercept satellite recently picked up a communication that we believe indicates the terrorists are now considering turning their deadly tactic against some unidentified stations in the region. Given our huge civilian population on these stations, the decision has been made to conduct a partial evacuation of all potential target stations. What we need from you is your help in getting these civilians – mostly the spouses and children of station personnel – to a station that is further away from the terrorists'' known area of operation. Normally, I would not ask this of a capsuleer, but I am begging you: will you help us evacuate these people until this threat has passed? We need to know right now, as we have already begun to organize the evacuation fleet; can we count you in?'),
(60011,'Two days ago, a covert Gallente strike team infiltrated and destroyed a brand new Command Center on a nearby ice planet. We think they managed to infiltrate as local civilian workers due the fact that the facility''s Personnel Security Identification Systems had not yet been fully brought online. This unforgivable lapse in security enabled the four-man team to gain access to a highly secure area that contains the controls for the counter-harmonic stabilizers which, in short, keep the entire facility level and secure in the very harsh climates encountered on that planet. A series of well-placed explosives damaged these stabilizers, however, taking them offline and causing the entire command center to collapse and sink through the ice to the ocean floor some two kilometers below. Fortunately, the bulk of the work force was not scheduled to arrive for two more weeks, so casualties were very light. The financial and economic costs were, however, staggering. Now that you understand the gravity of the situation, we can proceed to the reason that we contacted you to help us in this critical moment in the company''s ongoing rapid expansion phase. We need you to very quietly transport a company of our best Arctic Warfare Marines from this station to the destination station with all possible haste. From there they will flown to the ice planet to provide a very high level of security for this and other nearby command centers and facilities. It is just a matter of time before this disastrous event becomes public knowledge, and we need to prove to the senior management, shareholders, and investors that we have the security situation resolutely in hand. So, , are you willing to help us out by delivering a large number of Arctic Marines to the designated station?'),
(60012,'Yes, I think I have some work for you. One of our research outposts in Molden Heath came under attack by rogue drones last week. This is highly unusual, since drones are rarely seen beyond Etherium Reach. The outpost''s defense systems managed to keep our scientists safe, and the downed drones were retrieved for examination. They found unusual mineral deposits replacing the drones'' original microboard networks, which appear to work far more efficiently. Of course we don''t want anyone else getting ahold of the samples before we can replicate them. The samples have been in transit via a series of drops in order to keep them safe. Take them on to the labs at .'),
(60013,'''m not sure how much you know about Amarr slave labor installations, such as mines, agricultural harvesting fields, moon mineral extraction zones, and the like. Well, I can tell you that these facilities are often of such size and complexity that they cannot always be wholly secured against slave escape attempts. Certainly, all but the most primitive and poorly administrated of these locations feature any and all manner of perimeter alarms, security cameras, remote sentry drones, microwave motion detectors, infrared barrier fences, you name it. As you can imagine, though, this can get quite expensive given not only the capital outlay for the equipment, but for the manpower needed to operate and maintain them year-round, 24 hours a day. It was during this search for lower cost alternatives to these technologies that the animals we call slaver hounds were introduced to the overall security plans of select slave labor facilities, used to detect, track, and interdict runaway slaves. Their acutely tuned senses coupled with their remarkable natural endurance and speed made them an ideal choice for many Amarr slave operations. However, it was not long before it was realized that the standard, purebred slaver hound was not suitable for all environments. This resulted in the creation of genetically modified breeds more at home in harsher environments such as swamps, frozen wastelands, jungles, and the like. Today, these more adaptable variants can be found on many such installations throughout the Empire, despite their comparatively high cost when compared to your usual slaver hounds. This brings us to the reason I contacted you. I need a large shipment of these hybrid slaver hounds delivered to a nearby station for transshipment to an Amarr desert planet. As long as the hounds remain sedated and don''t find their way out of their cages, this should be a simple, trouble-free courier job.'),
(60014,'One of our Caldari Navy Special Forces units conducting clandestine reconnaissance of a contested ocean planet – a Gallente-claimed planet, by the way, with extremely rare seabed minerals – sent an emergency burst communication to the covert ops ship in orbit above the planet, requesting immediate extraction. This signal was, in turn, transmitted to the classified comms center here on this station. When we attempted to contact both the team and the ship, however, we received no response. Our immediate reaction was to divert one of our long range Crow-class interceptors, which was in the region on an unrelated mission, to investigate. Soon after its arrival, its sensors confirmed that the covert ops ship had been destroyed. There is nothing we can do for our lost covops ship; however, this series of events has left the Special Forces team alone and without a means to evacuate the planet. Even worse was a fragment from the original communication indicating that the team was on the run and low on food, water, weapons, and ammunition. They have taken refuge in a disused ocean mining facility, though it is doubtful that they will stay hidden for long. There simply aren''t many places to hide on that planet, given the fact that it is mostly covered by massive oceans, with very little land mass. It will not take long for the Gallente to track down our team and either kill them or, worse, capture them for interrogation. The good news in all this is that we have an extraction team in place, along with a shuttle-equipped vessel to deliver them to the planet. However, given the immediacy of this mission, they had to leave their original base without much of their usual equipment and weaponry. This is where you come in. We need you to transport several containers of highly specialized small arms and related equipment to the station at which the extraction team is currently located. Once you drop off this cargo, the team will gear-up and shuttle down to the planet to rescue the stranded team. So, pilot, what is it gonna be? Will you help us?'),
(60015,'History has shown us that a properly motivated slave work force can work harder and longer - especially in harsh conditions - if they are provided the means to enhance their everyday lives. Well, for many decades, the provision of various stimulant drugs to slave laborers was considered a standard method of doing business. However, the downside to this was that, while the use of stims typically increased productivity, more often than not it resulted in significant long term health problems for the slaves leading to shortened lifespans and, more importantly, to decreased profits. So, while the use of stimulants has largely been discontinued, the idea that drugs could increase slave output never entirely went away, though it did require a new approach. To this end, my company recently developed an inexpensive new drug that works on the pleasure centers of the brain, providing what we might call a “reward” for hard work. Importantly, this drug, known as Blue Paradise, or "Beep" as the techs call it, has been proven in real-world testing to increase slave labor output by as much as twenty percent across the board, without any known long term health problems. As you can guess, the increased profit potential here is, well, staggering. Equally important is the fact that we have not reported this new drug to the various control boards; nor do we intend to at this juncture. We need you to deliver a very large shipment of this drug to a forward logistics hub station from which it will be transshipped to ore mines, agricultural farms, and other slave-intensive operations. I can give you my guarantee that this cargo will not be flagged by customs or the police, as it is not yet deemed an illegal substance. So, can we count on you to deliver this?'),
(60016,'Our engineering scientists, working at our highly secure, clandestine RDfacility on a nearby planet have produced a new type of cloaking device that, when fitted to Covert Ops ships, could theoretically enable them to jump through stargates without uncloaking! And yes, I can see by the look on your face that you must think I''ve had far too many Extra Strength Quafe sodas today. However, I can assure you that, while it may be many years before this technology is perfected and suitable for even experimental use, the science behind it is quite real, and this is where this story takes a very important twist. Our internal security teams have managed to uncover a plan formulated by one of our competitors to steal the prototype cloaking system at some point between the time it leaves the lab up until it arrives at the field testing facility over in the next system. Problem is, we don''t yet know who the spy is, so we devised a plan to get that spy to expose himself so that we can then move in and make the arrest. To this end, you will be delivering is a very detailed mock-up series of the actual prototype, one that will withstand an initial visual and electronic scrutiny on the part of the thief. In all practical terms, however, these devices could no more cloak a ship than it could cook your morning breakfast. We are naming this event Operation Doorstop, which is our planning team''s attempt at humor, given the uselessness of this particular lump of metal and wires. What we do need, though, is your absolute confidentiality on this shipment. If the spy gets any whiff that this is a set-up, we will likely never know who he or she is, and we will remain at ongoing risk of one of our most important R&D projects potentially falling into the wrong hands. So, what do you say, ? Willing to take on this rather interesting assignment?'),
(60017,'One of our archaeological teams has unearthed a load of pre-Federation tech from a moon in this system. We''re really excited about this; I don''t think I need to explain to you how the results of this find could give us a leg up on the competition. Get this lot over to the labs at and don''t tell anyone!'),
(60018,'A severe accident has occurred on another station, ; they suffered a freak blowout in primary life-support and the station''s environmental control shut down entirely. No, don''t panic, they stabilized the atmosphere as soon as they could, so the people on the station won''t asphyxiate. But the internal heating units have yet to be replaced. People are bundling up as their heat bleeds out – the external insulation is some protection, but it''s not enough. To help out, we''ve put together as many portable emergency heating units as we could find on such short notice. Take them over to , and quickly!'),
(60019,'As you probably know all too well, speed is the lifeblood of the Republic''s defense fleets, particularly for the smaller frigates and cruisers. There''s a lot that goes into it: low-density reactor cores, kinesthetic maneuvering thrusters, hyper-responsive gyroscopic stabilizers. All the housings are built using nano-alloy rather than the more heavyweight materials the other empires use; it was simply more convenient back when the ships were first designed, but it gives them that little bit of extra boost that''s become our signature. Our R&D specialists have been working on a new formula for the C-86 thermal epoxy resin used on engine housings and other parts of the propulsion systems; I want you to take this batch over to for application and field testing.'),
(60020,'I''m sure you''re all too aware of our war with the Caldari State. It''s been dragging on for years with no end in sight... until now, that is. We''ve been making some good headway on the active front and our research and development has been busy behind the scenes. Military scientists have developed a hybrid round that works like single-target burst ECM, and it''s time to introduce it to the military for an active field-test. Take these over to .'),
(60021,'I''m in a bit of an awkward position here, . With all the people being released from slavery in the Empire, we''re getting more and more families who practice the Amarr religion. No thanks to Jamyl, she knew this would happen. The edict from our government is that we need to respect the poor deluded people and gently introduce them to a new way of thinking. It won''t be easy, and it''s putting a strain on all of us. My problem right now is that a bunch of the refugee families have requested that some Amarr Scriptures be included in the course structure at the schools we''ve set up for their children. It''s our own people doing the teaching, so we can slowly steer the education in the right direction, but we all still feel dirty for having to use it. Do you think you''d be willing to take a shipment of books over to one of the schools?'),
(60022,'Time is a factor here, so I will get to the point. The daughter of a prominent Caldari industrialist, CEO of a large scrap metal corporation, was kidnapped while she was on holiday with her school classmates. At the time of her abduction, she was in a lowsec system she should not have been in, one well known for its hedonistic night life. Apparently, the girls each told a bit of a fib to their parents, indicating they were traveling to a much safer, highsec destination resort. Well, early this morning we received an urgent call from the executive''s chief of security telling us that the daughter had been grabbed and thrown into a vehicle by some dangerous-looking men outside a bar after a night of drinking. While we had hoped it was part of some prank or a misunderstanding as to what the girls really saw, our worst fears have been realized. We have been contacted, through a circuitous channel, by a notorious band of slavers. As proof of life, they have transmitted the daughter''s DNA sequence to us. Analysis of this information has verified her identity. The kidnappers have given us a very short window in which we can secure the girl''s safe release, after which they will sell her into slavery – and I don''t want to even imagine what horrors that might entail. As expected, they are demanding a very large payoff in exchange for her life. Specifically, they want our entire stockpile of our rarest and most expensive metal, quantrium – one found only in the wiring of electronic countermeasures (ECM) equipment of the Caldari Navy''s Rook-class combat reconnaissance ships. What I need you to do is to quickly move this quantrium to the designated station for transshipment to the slavers'' rendezvous point. We will take it from there.'),
(60023,'This is a list of people I want you to escort to a meeting. They have quite a large security entourage, and as you can see from some of the names, they have a reason for it. These people are members of the Angel Cartel. While the Cartel are thugs and pirate scum, and are not particularly welcome in Minmatar space, it does not mean that some corporations don''t have certain dealings with them which require us to overlook certain... failings. Escort them safely to for me. It''s nothing you''ll be in trouble with the Republic for, but for the sake of our business relations, try to treat them politely. |collapsed= yes'),
(60024,'I have an important job for you, . Because of your good standing and the fact you have successfully completed a number of missions for we have decided you are worth the trust of a very important courier job. It entails bringing a large cargo of transaction and salary logs to this station from where they have been stored for the last few weeks for a routine inspection by the authorities. This data holds information of sensitive nature on our recent business dealings, earnings and expenses and wages that we pay our staff members. Under no circumstances may any of these reports be lost, or worse yet fall into the wrong hands. Pirates have a tendency to want this information so they can sell it to our rivals. They used to have easy access to this information by hacking our transmission calls, but now that we send these reports via freight this is no longer as serious of a problem. I trust you on this, , don''t let me down.'),
(60025,'Okay, here''s one for you. Don''t look at me like that. Yes, it''s a load of metal scraps we need taken to a reclamation facility at . Contrary to popular belief, our ships are not made solely of scrap-metal, utility adhesive and chewing gum, but we do recycle extensively. The reason I''m asking you to do this rather than hiring a much cheaper regular captain is that these bits are industrial quality, or they will be once they''ve been processed. They''re worth a lot of cred on the black market – peanuts to you capsuleers, but a year''s wages to anyone else.'),
(60026,'One of our subsidiaries has recently suffered a major setback, . A hurricane wiped out half their planetside crops and wrecked the equipment. Most of it was already falling apart, the storm just finished it off. Obviously, this is a big problem for them, and us, but it''s still the early part of the first growing season. Deliver these parts to the assembly plant at so we can replace the equipment before they lose too much from this harvest.'),
(60027,'Okay, take a look at this. You know what this is? Yes, yes, it''s a rock. It''s a rare mineral, actually, called Cerrocentite. It has industrial applications, but it''s mostly used in security systems. The reason it''s in a special containment field is that it''s also fairly radioactive. Take this shipment over to the manufacturers at , and don''t bloody open it!'),
(60028,'Two days ago, a covert Gallente strike team infiltrated and destroyed a brand new Command Center on a nearby ice planet. We think they managed to infiltrate as local civilian workers due the fact that the facility''s Personnel Security Identification Systems had not yet been fully brought online. This unforgivable lapse in security enabled the four-man team to gain access to a highly secure area that contains the controls for the counter-harmonic stabilizers which, in short, keep the entire facility level and secure in the very harsh climates encountered on that planet. A series of well-placed explosives damaged these stabilizers, however, taking them offline and causing the entire command center to collapse and sink through the ice to the ocean floor some two kilometers below. Fortunately, the bulk of the work force was not scheduled to arrive for two more weeks, so casualties were very light. The financial and economic costs were, however, staggering. Now that you understand the gravity of the situation, we can proceed to the reason that we contacted you to help us in this critical moment in the company''s ongoing rapid expansion phase. We need you to very quietly transport a company of our best Arctic Warfare Marines from this station to the destination station with all possible haste. From there they will flown to the ice planet to provide a very high level of security for this and other nearby command centers and facilities. It is just a matter of time before this disastrous event becomes public knowledge, and we need to prove to the senior management, shareholders, and investors that we have the security situation resolutely in hand. So, , are you willing to help us out by delivering a large number of Arctic Marines to the designated station?'),
(60029,'Yes, I think I have some work for you. One of our research outposts in Molden Heath came under attack by rogue drones last week. This is highly unusual, since drones are rarely seen beyond Etherium Reach. The outpost''s defense systems managed to keep our scientists safe, and the downed drones were retrieved for examination. They found unusual mineral deposits replacing the drones'' original microboard networks, which appear to work far more efficiently. Of course we don''t want anyone else getting ahold of the samples before we can replicate them. The samples have been in transit via a series of drops in order to keep them safe. Take them on to the labs at .'),
(60030,'History has shown us that a properly motivated slave work force can work harder and longer - especially in harsh conditions - if they are provided the means to enhance their everyday lives. Well, for many decades, the provision of various stimulant drugs to slave laborers was considered a standard method of doing business. However, the downside to this was that, while the use of stims typically increased productivity, more often than not it resulted in significant long term health problems for the slaves leading to shortened lifespans and, more importantly, to decreased profits. So, while the use of stimulants has largely been discontinued, the idea that drugs could increase slave output never entirely went away, though it did require a new approach. To this end, my company recently developed an inexpensive new drug that works on the pleasure centers of the brain, providing what we might call a “reward” for hard work. Importantly, this drug, known as Blue Paradise, or "Beep" as the techs call it, has been proven in real-world testing to increase slave labor output by as much as twenty percent across the board, without any known long term health problems. As you can guess, the increased profit potential here is, well, staggering. Equally important is the fact that we have not reported this new drug to the various control boards; nor do we intend to at this juncture. We need you to deliver a very large shipment of this drug to a forward logistics hub station from which it will be transshipped to ore mines, agricultural farms, and other slave-intensive operations. I can give you my guarantee that this cargo will not be flagged by customs or the police, as it is not yet deemed an illegal substance. So, can we count on you to deliver this?'),
(60031,'A severe accident has occurred on another station, ; they suffered a freak blowout in primary life-support and the station''s environmental control shut down entirely. No, don''t panic, they stabilized the atmosphere as soon as they could, so the people on the station won''t asphyxiate. But the internal heating units have yet to be replaced. People are bundling up as their heat bleeds out – the external insulation is some protection, but it''s not enough. To help out, we''ve put together as many portable emergency heating units as we could find on such short notice. Take them over to , and quickly!'),
(60032,'A few days ago, I was at one of those parties - you know the type, where they shoot you full of stims if you start to drag, and you just keep going until reality starts to fold in on itself and turn into confetti, and there''s the scent of rosewater and…. To make a long story short, I accidentally sent the wrong cargo over to . They were less than amused to receive a crate of live Intaki peepers rather than the cryo-stored Luminaire skippers they needed. One frog is much like another, but the pet-shop variety make very poor laboratory testing groups. Take these over, and they may forgive me enough to require my services in the future. |collapsed= yes'),
(60033,'Greetings, . Several days ago, an internal security team identified a Gallente deep cover saboteur working at one of our clandestine shipyards producing the current generation of Widow-class Black Ops battleships. He swallowed a hidden poison tablet as we moved in to arrest him, so he is no longer a threat. However, during a routine quality control check, the shipyard''s scientific team was shocked to discover a highly advanced nanite swarm that the saboteur had somehow introduced into the shipyard''s stockpile of advanced adhesives used to bond sensor-absorbing coatings to the hulls of our newly-constructed Widows. The effect of this harmful agent is to slowly erode this protective coating, thus increasing the ship''s signature radius, making it much easier for our enemies to detect and attack. Given the slow-acting nature of this particular breed of nanite, it is unlikely that this gradual loss of stealth capability would be noticeable under routine operating conditions, thus placing the ship and its crew at mortal risk when operating in hostile space. Essentially, the Widow''s commander would not know that his ship had lost its critical operational advantage until he was detected and targeted by hostile combatants. Given the very specialized role of this ship, not only would the Widow be compromised, but it is possible than any ships he might be bridging in via its covert jump portal generator could be unknowingly hot dropped near a waiting enemy fleet, instead of empty space. In order to remedy this critical situation, we need you to immediately transport a large quantity of our new aerogel counteragent to a station for further distribution to the fleet. This shipment represents our best and only hope to quickly repair the damage done by the Gallente spy and ensure the safety of our brave Widow pilots and crew.'),
(60034,'A short time ago, Minmatar terrorists in a combined fleet of frigates and cruisers attacked one of our Harbinger-class battlecruisers as it was transporting slaves from a recently closed mine to a new mineral harvesting facility in a nearby system. While all but one of the attackers was annihilated, our convoy''s escorts were destroyed and our cruiser is burning. Making a bad situation worse, we are anticipating that the terrorists will return in force within the next several hours to attempt the theft of our slaves, as they almost certainly know the cruiser is alone and all but helpless. Our concern is that if the terrorists feel that they have a window of opportunity to recover these slaves, it is likely that they will throw everything they have into the effort. Our intelligence assessments of the terrorists'' fleet assets are even less reassuring: we believe that they could send as many as four battlecruisers into this fight – more than enough to wipe out the arriving frigates and forcefully board our heavily damaged strategic cruiser. However, we have calculated that if we can delay any terrorist boarding parties long enough, this should give us enough time for the much larger main rescue fleet to arrive. The only bright side to this situation, in what is unquestionably an act of divine providence, is that a large contingent of marines are aboard this station as we speak, having just completed specialized refresher training in counter-boarding operations. We need you to deliver them to the station closest to the last reported position of our cruiser. From there, we will transport a combined team of marines, engineers, medics, and other essential personnel to hopefully stop the fire and save the ship - along with its cargo of highly valuable slaves. However, this mission must be undertaken immediately. Any delay will surely doom the Harbinger and her brave crew.'),
(60035,'I have an important job for you, . Because of your good standing and the fact you have successfully completed a number of missions for we have decided you are worth the trust of a very important courier job. It entails bringing a large cargo of transaction and salary logs to this station from where they have been stored for the last few weeks for a routine inspection by the authorities. This data holds information of sensitive nature on our recent business dealings, earnings and expenses and wages that we pay our staff members. Under no circumstances may any of these reports be lost, or worse yet fall into the wrong hands. Pirates have a tendency to want this information so they can sell it to our rivals. They used to have easy access to this information by hacking our transmission calls, but now that we send these reports via freight this is no longer as serious of a problem. I trust you on this, , don''t let me down.'),
(60036,'"HI know the security screening process at this station has been time-consuming and a bit, well, intrusive. Now that you have passed our various tests, however, I feel confident that I can now let you in on the reason you are here. One of our regional governors had recently been planning an unannounced visit to one of the new planetary command centers in a nearby system. For security reasons, this information was restricted to only those in the governor''s inner circle, to include the commander of his personal security detail. Well, this commander decided to test his internal security prior to this event, to best ensure the governor''s safe travel. So, for this exercise, he created a painstakingly detailed agenda, identical in every detail to an actual state visit. In this scenario, the governor was to travel by chartered high-speed maglev train to a number of the new planetary command centers. As the Governor''s decoy train traveled through a large canyon, however, a series of explosive charges detonated on the rail line, sending the train off its track and into the canyon wall. As it turned out, the security commander''s ruse had worked perfectly; someone in the governor''s inner circle had tipped his or her hand and provided information to unknown assassins. So far, however, we have not been able to determine the traitor''s identity, and each member of the inner circle is vehemently denying any involvement, despite our best chemical interrogations. So, what this investigation will likely boil down to is to what clues can be solved from the train wreckage, the destroyed maglev track sections, and the soil around the site of the blasts. We need you to transport several investigative teams, along with a considerable amount of equipment, to a nearby station where they will then be transported via shuttle to the planet. Will you take on this mission?'),
(60037,'Earlier today, a small, unknown group of frigates attacked one of our remote signals intelligence (SIGINT) communications outposts, causing catastrophic damage and killing dozens of our personnel. This station belongs – or should I say belonged - to a small Caldari corporation with a poorly hidden contractual link to our military intelligence services. Fortunately, the survivors managed to escape, via their high-speed emergency shuttle and are expected to arrive at a nearby station within the hour. As you might expect, we are working hard to determine the identities of the aggressors, but as yet we have no solid leads. Of course, this is not your concern. What is your concern, should you choose to help us, is a report we just received indicating that the surviving team of SIGINT contractors have been targeted for immediate assassination by the same mysterious organization behind the outpost attack. Apparently, someone does not want these individuals to provide us with whatever information they must have obtained during the course of their recent duties. Within the last few hours, we intercepted a poorly encrypted communication indicating that a covert hit squad is en route to the station aboard an unspecified vessel – or may actually be at the station already! This station''s security force, while well armed and highly trained, is insufficient to detect and defeat the kind of lethal operatives that we believe intend to kill our contractors. Therefore, we need you to rescue this team immediately and bring them back to us for an emergency debriefing and to ensure their safety. After running a check of qualified pilots in our office database, your name was near the top of the list. We estimate there will only be sufficient time for this one rescue attempt before the assassins strike.'),
(60038,'I have a very special mission for you today, . A high-ranked Overseer of a secret compound in has requested items of ours that must be delivered to him A.S.A.P. This job must be done in complete secrecy; we do not want the contents of this delivery to fall into the wrong hands. As a precautionary measure, we have set up an explosive mechanism inside the cargo containers that will trigger should anyone attempt to tamper with them. I trust you on this, . Be very discreet and, at any cost, avoid confrontation with hostiles en route to your destination. Make haste!'),
(60039,'"! Glad you could make it on such short notice. Let me get right to the point: Yesterday, as you almost certainly know, a regional governor delivered her State of the Region address. Needless to say, we were quite excited and thus put forth a maximum effort to ensure that her speech was broadcast on every possible channel and to the maximum ranges of our civilian and military communications networks. However, for various reasons at many remote locations, this signal did not reach many who would have otherwise benefitted from this opportunity. For all our efforts, there are some locations that can only be reached the hard way -- ferrying holoreels directly to each and every one of them. We have already dispatched messengers, primarily in interceptors and other fast ships, to these more dangerous destinations. We need you to transport a quantity of holoreels containing the State of the Region speech to one station in particular and hand them over to an agent who will be waiting for them there. He will then handle all further distribution of the ''reels. So, can you help us with what should be a straightforward courier job?'),
(60040,'You need to keep this quiet, . I know you capsuleers aren''t accustomed to being told how to do your job, but this is bigger than anything else and if word gets out, all this effort will be for nothing. We''ve acquired samples of the Amarr''s latest experimental starship tech. Don''t ask me how, I don''t want to know, and neither do you. We''re not sure what these pieces do; our source is suggesting it''s a system that reduces the effectiveness of our electronic warfare systems. This could be bad news for us. Get the stuff over to the lab at . And keep your trap shut. We don''t want it getting back to the Amarr that we have this.'),
(60041,'One of my clients asked me to send over drones to replace the ones his company''s been losing in the line of work. That''s all he said. He never said anything about needing mining drones; of course I sent him a set of scout drones, and he was very upset at me for not being able to read his mind. People should be more specific about things. Take these mining drones over to for him, and if he asks why the paint looks new, tell him they''re fresh off the production line.'),
(60042,'Let me start at the beginning. As you have probably seen on the news channels, a prominent Caldari mining company is in the middle of a very nasty battle for economic survival with a new, up-and-coming mining company from within the same large conglomerate. Both of these companies specialize in the extraction of ores from some of the more inhospitable and dangerous locations in this and several adjoining systems. While this can be hazardous with regard to men and equipment, the profit potential from these largely untapped ore reserves can be quite significant, which brings me to our current predicament. As you may know, the specialized manual labor required for some of these mines can be significant in terms of numbers. Well, the Mining Health and Safety Commission, or MHSC, for this region recently conducted a survey of the first company''s operations, and found that their mining practices at certain locations may have resulted in excessive pollution, then further alleged a corresponding link to long-term miner health problems. The company has loudly complained that this is a ridiculous witch hunt brought about by their new competitor, which happens to have several “friends” on the commission. While they work to ensure they are equally “represented” on that commission, the recent finding has mandated that they immediately improve worker conditions and reduce pollution or risk losing their mining rights. To remedy this problem, they recently purchased a large number of the latest environmentally-friendly – and obscenely expensive – manportable drills, which seems to have assuaged the MHSC for the moment. They do, however, have a deadline for actually putting these new drills into the hands of the miners, which brings us to the reason I contacted you. We need you to deliver a rather large shipment of drills and other related equipment to a station that serves as a central service hub. From there, logistics pilots will deliver this and other items to the various mines in the system. Will you take on this important job?'),
(60043,'I like nice things, . Who doesn''t? Handing missions out to you people all day doesn''t offer nearly enough to cover my expenses, so a friend and I run a shipping business out to Syndicate space. Nothing big enough to interfere with the Syndicate itself, mind you. We provide a humanitarian service importing the latest holos from the heart of civilization. It''s the only way they can get the things for a reasonable cost – buying them direct from the companies in the Federation incurs immense shipping charges. Our usual courier is out of commission today, with her ship in for repairs after a pirate attack. If you want to make yourself useful, take the latest shipment over to and ask for Amelyn. They''ll know who you mean, just say that “Imba” sent you.'),
(60044,'We have several research outposts in various w-space systems. It''s one of those things that nobody discusses but everybody knows about anyway. They''ve recovered bits of ancient technology which seem to have unusual properties... well, compared to what we''re used to seeing, at least. We''re hoping these might be a clue to the Sleepers'' technology... but it could easily be remnants of a scrapyard, for all we know. Take these samples over to the lab at , so we can figure out what we''ve got.'),
(60045,'I''m sure you''re all too aware of our war with the Caldari State. It''s been dragging on for years with no end in sight... until now, that is. We''ve been making some good headway on the active front and our research and development has been busy behind the scenes. Military scientists have developed a hybrid round that works like single-target burst ECM, and it''s time to introduce it to the military for an active field-test. Take these over to .'),
(60046,'I''m in a bit of an awkward position here, . With all the people being released from slavery in the Empire, we''re getting more and more families who practice the Amarr religion. No thanks to Jamyl, she knew this would happen. The edict from our government is that we need to respect the poor deluded people and gently introduce them to a new way of thinking. It won''t be easy, and it''s putting a strain on all of us. My problem right now is that a bunch of the refugee families have requested that some Amarr Scriptures be included in the course structure at the schools we''ve set up for their children. It''s our own people doing the teaching, so we can slowly steer the education in the right direction, but we all still feel dirty for having to use it. Do you think you''d be willing to take a shipment of books over to one of the schools?'),
(60047,'Last night, a strike team of suicide terrorists from the Anti-Corporatist Revolutionary Front, or ARCF, struck at more than twenty Caldari offices and stations throughout the region. During one of these attacks a terrorist was captured with a well-shielded, improvised nuclear device hidden in his rucksack. Obviously this event represents an entirely new level of threat from the ARCF, now that they have proven themselves willing to carry out such a horrendous and indiscriminate mass casualty attack. The only upside to this is that the terrorist has turned out to be the most notorious operative of the ARCF, a woman known as Commander Rachendia. Having her in custody has offered us an opportunity to gain information related to her group''s future plans to strike at the Caldari State. During one of the more aggressive interrogations, she disclosed information about a pending attack against one of our nearby stations. The nature of the attack is not entirely clear; however, we know with certainty that it involves the surreptitious introduction of a viral agent into the life support and air circulation systems. Our initial searches for these hidden canisters at that station have, so far, been fruitless – with the exception of one small aerosol-type canister. A preliminary test revealed that these viral weapons appear to be based on a self-replicating nanotechnology. Once released from stasis in their container, they seek out and consume human tissue, and leaving behind little more than dust. Our medical scientists have calculated that just one container, released into the central air processing vents, could result in the deaths of all human life aboard a medium-sized station within no more than four hours. The only good news is that these nanos are programmed to self-terminate within 12 hours. Of course, this would be far more time than would be necessary to kill everyone aboard all but the largest of stations. Your role in this desperate situation is to deliver a cargo of electromagnetic weapons, modified to emit a short-range pulse that will literally "fry" any nanos within its range. So, we are asking: will you deliver these containers to the station immediately? Thousands of lives may depend on your answer.'),
(60048,'Time is a factor here, so I will get to the point. The daughter of a prominent Caldari industrialist, CEO of a large scrap metal corporation, was kidnapped while she was on holiday with her school classmates. At the time of her abduction, she was in a lowsec system she should not have been in, one well known for its hedonistic night life. Apparently, the girls each told a bit of a fib to their parents, indicating they were traveling to a much safer, highsec destination resort. Well, early this morning we received an urgent call from the executive''s chief of security telling us that the daughter had been grabbed and thrown into a vehicle by some dangerous-looking men outside a bar after a night of drinking. While we had hoped it was part of some prank or a misunderstanding as to what the girls really saw, our worst fears have been realized. We have been contacted, through a circuitous channel, by a notorious band of slavers. As proof of life, they have transmitted the daughter''s DNA sequence to us. Analysis of this information has verified her identity. The kidnappers have given us a very short window in which we can secure the girl''s safe release, after which they will sell her into slavery – and I don''t want to even imagine what horrors that might entail. As expected, they are demanding a very large payoff in exchange for her life. Specifically, they want our entire stockpile of our rarest and most expensive metal, quantrium – one found only in the wiring of electronic countermeasures (ECM) equipment of the Caldari Navy''s Rook-class combat reconnaissance ships. What I need you to do is to quickly move this quantrium to the designated station for transshipment to the slavers'' rendezvous point. We will take it from there.'),
(60049,'I have a very special mission for you today, . A high-ranked Overseer of a secret compound in has requested items of ours that must be delivered to him A.S.A.P. This job must be done in complete secrecy; we do not want the contents of this delivery to fall into the wrong hands. As a precautionary measure, we have set up an explosive mechanism inside the cargo containers that will trigger should anyone attempt to tamper with them. I trust you on this, . Be very discreet and, at any cost, avoid confrontation with hostiles en route to your destination. Make haste!'),
(60050,'Two days ago, a covert Gallente strike team infiltrated and destroyed a brand new Command Center on a nearby ice planet. We think they managed to infiltrate as local civilian workers due the fact that the facility''s Personnel Security Identification Systems had not yet been fully brought online. This unforgivable lapse in security enabled the four-man team to gain access to a highly secure area that contains the controls for the counter-harmonic stabilizers which, in short, keep the entire facility level and secure in the very harsh climates encountered on that planet. A series of well-placed explosives damaged these stabilizers, however, taking them offline and causing the entire command center to collapse and sink through the ice to the ocean floor some two kilometers below. Fortunately, the bulk of the work force was not scheduled to arrive for two more weeks, so casualties were very light. The financial and economic costs were, however, staggering. Now that you understand the gravity of the situation, we can proceed to the reason that we contacted you to help us in this critical moment in the company''s ongoing rapid expansion phase. We need you to very quietly transport a company of our best Arctic Warfare Marines from this station to the destination station with all possible haste. From there they will flown to the ice planet to provide a very high level of security for this and other nearby command centers and facilities. It is just a matter of time before this disastrous event becomes public knowledge, and we need to prove to the senior management, shareholders, and investors that we have the security situation resolutely in hand. So, , are you willing to help us out by delivering a large number of Arctic Marines to the designated station?'),
(60051,'Yes, I think I have some work for you. One of our research outposts in Molden Heath came under attack by rogue drones last week. This is highly unusual, since drones are rarely seen beyond Etherium Reach. The outpost''s defense systems managed to keep our scientists safe, and the downed drones were retrieved for examination. They found unusual mineral deposits replacing the drones'' original microboard networks, which appear to work far more efficiently. Of course we don''t want anyone else getting ahold of the samples before we can replicate them. The samples have been in transit via a series of drops in order to keep them safe. Take them on to the labs at .'),
(60052,'History has shown us that a properly motivated slave work force can work harder and longer - especially in harsh conditions - if they are provided the means to enhance their everyday lives. Well, for many decades, the provision of various stimulant drugs to slave laborers was considered a standard method of doing business. However, the downside to this was that, while the use of stims typically increased productivity, more often than not it resulted in significant long term health problems for the slaves leading to shortened lifespans and, more importantly, to decreased profits. So, while the use of stimulants has largely been discontinued, the idea that drugs could increase slave output never entirely went away, though it did require a new approach. To this end, my company recently developed an inexpensive new drug that works on the pleasure centers of the brain, providing what we might call a “reward” for hard work. Importantly, this drug, known as Blue Paradise, or "Beep" as the techs call it, has been proven in real-world testing to increase slave labor output by as much as twenty percent across the board, without any known long term health problems. As you can guess, the increased profit potential here is, well, staggering. Equally important is the fact that we have not reported this new drug to the various control boards; nor do we intend to at this juncture. We need you to deliver a very large shipment of this drug to a forward logistics hub station from which it will be transshipped to ore mines, agricultural farms, and other slave-intensive operations. I can give you my guarantee that this cargo will not be flagged by customs or the police, as it is not yet deemed an illegal substance. So, can we count on you to deliver this?'),
(60053,'A severe accident has occurred on another station, ; they suffered a freak blowout in primary life-support and the station''s environmental control shut down entirely. No, don''t panic, they stabilized the atmosphere as soon as they could, so the people on the station won''t asphyxiate. But the internal heating units have yet to be replaced. People are bundling up as their heat bleeds out – the external insulation is some protection, but it''s not enough. To help out, we''ve put together as many portable emergency heating units as we could find on such short notice. Take them over to , and quickly!'),
(60054,'A few days ago, I was at one of those parties - you know the type, where they shoot you full of stims if you start to drag, and you just keep going until reality starts to fold in on itself and turn into confetti, and there''s the scent of rosewater and…. To make a long story short, I accidentally sent the wrong cargo over to . They were less than amused to receive a crate of live Intaki peepers rather than the cryo-stored Luminaire skippers they needed. One frog is much like another, but the pet-shop variety make very poor laboratory testing groups. Take these over, and they may forgive me enough to require my services in the future. |collapsed= yes'),
(60055,'Greetings, . Several days ago, an internal security team identified a Gallente deep cover saboteur working at one of our clandestine shipyards producing the current generation of Widow-class Black Ops battleships. He swallowed a hidden poison tablet as we moved in to arrest him, so he is no longer a threat. However, during a routine quality control check, the shipyard''s scientific team was shocked to discover a highly advanced nanite swarm that the saboteur had somehow introduced into the shipyard''s stockpile of advanced adhesives used to bond sensor-absorbing coatings to the hulls of our newly-constructed Widows. The effect of this harmful agent is to slowly erode this protective coating, thus increasing the ship''s signature radius, making it much easier for our enemies to detect and attack. Given the slow-acting nature of this particular breed of nanite, it is unlikely that this gradual loss of stealth capability would be noticeable under routine operating conditions, thus placing the ship and its crew at mortal risk when operating in hostile space. Essentially, the Widow''s commander would not know that his ship had lost its critical operational advantage until he was detected and targeted by hostile combatants. Given the very specialized role of this ship, not only would the Widow be compromised, but it is possible than any ships he might be bridging in via its covert jump portal generator could be unknowingly hot dropped near a waiting enemy fleet, instead of empty space. In order to remedy this critical situation, we need you to immediately transport a large quantity of our new aerogel counteragent to a station for further distribution to the fleet. This shipment represents our best and only hope to quickly repair the damage done by the Gallente spy and ensure the safety of our brave Widow pilots and crew.'),
(60056,'A short time ago, Minmatar terrorists in a combined fleet of frigates and cruisers attacked one of our Harbinger-class battlecruisers as it was transporting slaves from a recently closed mine to a new mineral harvesting facility in a nearby system. While all but one of the attackers was annihilated, our convoy''s escorts were destroyed and our cruiser is burning. Making a bad situation worse, we are anticipating that the terrorists will return in force within the next several hours to attempt the theft of our slaves, as they almost certainly know the cruiser is alone and all but helpless. Our concern is that if the terrorists feel that they have a window of opportunity to recover these slaves, it is likely that they will throw everything they have into the effort. Our intelligence assessments of the terrorists'' fleet assets are even less reassuring: we believe that they could send as many as four battlecruisers into this fight – more than enough to wipe out the arriving frigates and forcefully board our heavily damaged strategic cruiser. However, we have calculated that if we can delay any terrorist boarding parties long enough, this should give us enough time for the much larger main rescue fleet to arrive. The only bright side to this situation, in what is unquestionably an act of divine providence, is that a large contingent of marines are aboard this station as we speak, having just completed specialized refresher training in counter-boarding operations. We need you to deliver them to the station closest to the last reported position of our cruiser. From there, we will transport a combined team of marines, engineers, medics, and other essential personnel to hopefully stop the fire and save the ship - along with its cargo of highly valuable slaves. However, this mission must be undertaken immediately. Any delay will surely doom the Harbinger and her brave crew.'),
(60057,'Okay, take a look at this. You know what this is? Yes, yes, it''s a rock. It''s a rare mineral, actually, called Cerrocentite. It has industrial applications, but it''s mostly used in security systems. The reason it''s in a special containment field is that it''s also fairly radioactive. Take this shipment over to the manufacturers at , and don''t bloody open it!'),
(60058,'I have an important job for you, . Because of your good standing and the fact you have successfully completed a number of missions for we have decided you are worth the trust of a very important courier job. It entails bringing a large cargo of transaction and salary logs to this station from where they have been stored for the last few weeks for a routine inspection by the authorities. This data holds information of sensitive nature on our recent business dealings, earnings and expenses and wages that we pay our staff members. Under no circumstances may any of these reports be lost, or worse yet fall into the wrong hands. Pirates have a tendency to want this information so they can sell it to our rivals. They used to have easy access to this information by hacking our transmission calls, but now that we send these reports via freight this is no longer as serious of a problem. I trust you on this, , don''t let me down.'),
(60059,'You are aware, no doubt, of the rumors of extremist antislavery terrorist groups within the Amarr Empire itself. Well, you know then that their loyalty to the Empire is indeed secondary to their overarching desire to see all slaves freed and made equal members of society. This is a condition that we, as the greatest state in all of New Eden, simply cannot tolerate. However, our efforts at arresting and reeducating those insurgents have largely failed to permanently change the mindsets of these rather fanatical individuals. This system has been particularly hard hit by this and other like-minded groups. Most recently, an Anathema-class covert ops ship, specially configured to transport elite slaves to the estates of senior Amarr leaders in the region, was somehow decloaked, its weapons and sensors jammed, and ruthlessly attacked to the point of near-total structure failure. The terrorists then demanded the pilot transfer the slaves to this mystery ship, on threat of the total destruction of the covert ops vessel. The pilot complied, though he has since been punished for his cowardice. It is for this reason that I called you here today. I need you to transport a new shipment of elite slaves to a nearby station for further transshipment to the residence of one of the regional governors. This shipment is of particular urgency as the governor is hosting his annual gala event at his estate, and the usual staff of slaves simply will not do. We need these specific slaves, as they have been trained in protocol, proper food and drink service, entertainment, and numerous other talents that I need not mention here. Will you take on this courier mission on behalf of the Empire and deliver these highly trained and extremely expensive slaves to the designated station?'),
(60060,'"! Glad you could make it on such short notice. Let me get right to the point: Yesterday, as you almost certainly know, a regional governor delivered her State of the Region address. Needless to say, we were quite excited and thus put forth a maximum effort to ensure that her speech was broadcast on every possible channel and to the maximum ranges of our civilian and military communications networks. However, for various reasons at many remote locations, this signal did not reach many who would have otherwise benefitted from this opportunity. For all our efforts, there are some locations that can only be reached the hard way -- ferrying holoreels directly to each and every one of them. We have already dispatched messengers, primarily in interceptors and other fast ships, to these more dangerous destinations. We need you to transport a quantity of holoreels containing the State of the Region speech to one station in particular and hand them over to an agent who will be waiting for them there. He will then handle all further distribution of the ''reels. So, can you help us with what should be a straightforward courier job?'),
(60061,'I have a very special mission for you today, . A high-ranked Overseer of a secret compound in has requested items of ours that must be delivered to him A.S.A.P. This job must be done in complete secrecy; we do not want the contents of this delivery to fall into the wrong hands. As a precautionary measure, we have set up an explosive mechanism inside the cargo containers that will trigger should anyone attempt to tamper with them. I trust you on this, . Be very discreet and, at any cost, avoid confrontation with hostiles en route to your destination. Make haste!'),
(60074,'Alright, here''s a job you might be ready to tackle. A few unfortunate members of our corporation were kidnapped yesterday while on duty near the edge of this very system. I have reliable information that their kidnappers are nearby. I''ll upload the coordinates into your NeoCom: You should use them to find a series of gateways which should lead you to these enemies of the state. Sound like something you''d be interested in? If you succeed I will reward you handsomely.'),
(60075,'Our counter-intelligence service has indicated that the Gallente Federal Intelligence Office has erected a covert listening post in . While I assure you our communications are encrypted, the presence of Gallente intelligence operations in our space poses both an insult to Caldari sovereignty and an unacceptable risk to communications security. Your task is simple: go there, overwhelm whatever forces are defending the post, and destroy it. Can I count on you to see this through?'),
(60076,'I have just the thing you want. Ah, , good to see you. To business. We''ve just detected a hidden Amarrian reconaissance outpost nearby. I don''t need to explain the threat to you, do I? We must wipe them out before they are able to expand their operations further into our territory. If you can take care of this problem for me, you will be well rewarded.'),
(60078,'A slave named Jaliti has escaped from the house of the one of the five Heirs to the Imperial Throne. We don''t know why or how, but she has commandeered a luxury transport and is still on the run. The Heir in question, who will of course remain anonymous, demands her return, for he greatly enjoys her beauty and company. She is also privy to a great number of personal secrets that could cause great embarrassment to the Heir, and perhaps even to the Imperial Council. We intercepted a transmission indicating that she intends to meet a contact in the system. We don''t know whom she will meet, but you must stop her and bring her back, any way you can. Alive, if possible, but dead if necessary. I''m sure if you''re successful, the rewards will be substantial. We are dealing with an Heir, after all. The ship Jaliti commandeered is known to be well-armed. You might need a battle-ready frigate to bring her back.'),
(60080,'The time has come to strike a blow against the arrogant Gallente. We''re going to stage a raid deep into Gallente territory. In order to mask the movements of our forces, however, we first need to wipe out their pickets and patrols. We could do this with our own ships, of course, but that might alert the enemy to our plans. A lone, talented capsuleer, on the other hand, would make short work of them and raise less suspicion. I''ve uploaded the coordinates of the stepping-off point of our raid into your nav-computer. I want you to go there and destroy all of the enemy ships you find. Be advised that they may try to bring in reinforcements, but that should be no problem for someone of your caliber. Are you up to the task?'),
(60081,'A Caldari envoy is soliciting our assistance for his particular area of space. However, his transport ship is poorly guarded. Meet him at and escort him the rest of the way here.'),
(60082,', we''ve spotted a few Angel Cartel ships roaming about near here. We believe that they are part of a reconnaissance force sent to scout for a weakness in security, probably in preparation for a drug-smuggling operation. We sent a few of our best men out to intercept them, but none have returned. Another surveillance team caught sight of them again recently, though, and decided to wait for someone a bit more competent before we engage them again. I''m hoping you will be up to the task of taking out these scoundrels. The Angels are led by an infamous captain, of whom you may have heard already: Jenmai Hirokan. Do not underestimate him! Many have done so in the past and have paid the ultimate price. I won''t keep you here any longer. I''m sure you''ll want to get going before we lose sight of Hirokan and his allies again.'),
(60083,', we''ve spotted a few Blood Raider ships roaming about near here. We believe that they are part of a reconnaissance force sent to scout for a weakness in security, probably in preparation for a raid on one of our outlying settlements. We sent a few of our best men out to intercept them, but none have returned. Another surveillance team caught sight of them again recently, though, and decided to wait for someone a bit more competent before we engage them again. I''m hoping you will be up to the task of taking out these scoundrels. The Raiders are led by an infamous captain, of whom you may have heard already: Her name is Uleen Bloodsworn. Do not underestimate her! Many have done so in the past and have paid the ultimate price. I won''t keep you here any longer. I''m sure you''ll want to get going before we lose sight of Bloodsworn and her allies again.'),
(60084,', we''ve spotted a few Serpentis ships roaming about near here. We believe that they are part of a reconnaissance force sent to scout for a raid on one of our outlying settlements in . We sent a few of our best men out to intercept them, but none have returned. Another surveillance team caught sight of them again recently, though, and decided to wait for someone a bit more competent before we engage them again. I''m hoping you will be up to the task of taking out these scoundrels. The raiders are led by an infamous captain, of whom you may have heard already: His name is Jarkon Puman. Do not underestimate him! Many have done so in the past and have paid the ultimate price. I won''t keep you here any longer. I''m sure you''ll want to get going before we lose sight of Puman and his allies again.'),
(60086,'In the last few weeks, we''ve become aware of an FTL transmitter in the area which has been broadcasting anti-corporate propaganda into the State. Usually, the Federation isn''t quite this bold in its slander of our state, so a number of corporate intelligence offices looked into the matter and found to our surprise that this transmitter is actually being run by someone we are all too familiar with: Melarius Torvil and his so-called “Brothers of Freedom.” Obviously, we cannot allow this situation to continue. Torvil''s persistent ability to elude capture by Caldari authorities is frustrating enough, but we cannot simply stand by while he rubs it in our faces. Frankly, the fact that the Republic is allowing this kind of dangerous nonsense makes me thankful our militia capsuleers are giving them a hard time. Anyway, we would like you to fly to the transmitter in Hageken: Destroy it and any Minmatar vessels in the area. If the Republic Navy sends any ships to assist, feel free to eliminate them as well, but it isn''t necessary; I don''t think they''ll be willing to stick their necks out over what is a rather diplomatically shady activity anyway. What do you say? Can you handle this for me?'),
(60087,'In the past several months, several cruise ships carrying close to 100,000 Amarr citizens have vanished without a trace. Of course, we first believed these disappearances to be accidents. We enlisted the help of several ISK-strapped capsuleers to poke around neighboring systems and scan the planets and moons for something. One of these pilots discovered a Blood Raider installation in a system three jumps from the last known transport ship disappearance. Over the local comms channels, this brave pilot overheard the Raiders refer to it as a "Blood Farm." We know now that the ships were hijacked and our citizens taken to this installation. There, they were systematically butchered. I need you to go to this Blood Farm and eliminate anything that even smells like a Blood Raider operation. Don''t stop until every last heretic has been utterly and completely destroyed. If there are any tourists still alive, bring them home.'),
(60091,'Hang on, I need to finish this call. Really, another one? That same station, huh? Well, I don''t know what the capsuleer was flying. What do you want me to do, hold their hands? No, don''t even joke about that. One more? Do you really think it''s going to be any different? Okay, but don''t blame me if this one fails, too. Okay now, where were we? Oh, yes, the exciting opportunity I have for you today! It''s a bit run-of-the-mill, but I think you''ve earned an easy one, friend. It''s just a tiny little rogue drone problem. There couldn''t be more than half a dozen of the little bastards. I''ll bet if you just zip in there and rattle off a few shots at the infested station, they''ll scatter like frightened children. What do you say?'),
(60092,'A Gallente admiral has seen the light of true faith and experienced a religious conversion. A hand-written, hand-delivered letter — on actual paper! — arrived in the office this morning, expressing Admiral Meledier''s desire to defect. Having a high-ranking Gallente officer suddenly join our side could cause tremendous damage to the ability of their capsuleers to wage war against us: His knowledge of their systems and tactics would be staggering. We want you to go collect him from the rendezvous point in . You game?'),
(60093,'Ah, , I''m glad to see you received my mail. I have something that requires complete discretion. It''s entirely legal of course, but this will need to be kept quiet all the same. You''ve proven yourself trustworthy, so if you want the assignment I''ll hand it over to you. During a routine system scan, some of my people stumbled upon something that may be a significant archaeological find. I can''t just call in anyone to confirm it, though, that would risk a leak. I don''t want anyone else claiming this discovery as their own, especially if it turns out to be a lucrative one. What we could do is rig your vessel''s camera drones to relay a live feed of the site back to me and a friend of mine at the House of Records. From there, my friend would be able to direct you around the area to observe places of interest. What you relay back could help us confirm or disprove our earlier findings. The site is in Sarekuwa, so you wouldn''t be travelling very far to investigate, either. Our scouts reported there was a light pirate presence, and interference was making the use of microwarpdrives impossible in there, but I''m sure you can deal with a few Guristas and using afterburner. Not the usual assignment I know, but one of potentially great importance...and profit. It would be ideal if we could rely on capsuleer assistance for this. What do you say?'),
(60096,'I''m glad to see you made it over, [Player Name]. I have a problem with some Gallente miners that I think you''d be perfect for. The Gallente have set up another mining operation near one of our asteroid belts. They bring in semi-mobile reprocessing stations and then mine the location dry. You have to recognize this as just another act of war, Thocksan. Chief Executive Panel has lost millions of ISK to these Federation parasites. It''s almost as damaging as a direct attack, but it doesn''t draw the sort of military response an overt assault would, which is why we need capsuleer assistance to deal with this quickly. We know they''ve set up mining outpost at one of the smaller deadspace asteroid pockets Chief Executive Panel frequents. They do this in the hope that nobody will come after them. I need you to send the Federation a message that they''re wrong – that the State will pursue them every time. You must show them that there''s no profit to be made from illegally mining belts we have claimed. Go to the outpost and destroy absolutely everything; all the miners and any reprocessing stations you see. Level the place entirely. The loss of personnel and equipment will set them back and send a clear message to stick to their own space.'),
(60097,'Only a few moments ago the CEO from one of our subsidiaries was attacked and ransomed by Guristas, right in front of our trade delegation. Local security forces were overwhelmed and the pirates managed to escape. Our scouts pursued the Guristas vessels back to a Federation detention facility, which suggests the Guristas are only acting as mercenaries and the Gallente are really the ones to blame. We have scouts holding above the detention facility, and they''re tapping communications to look for evidence of a connection, but in the meantime we want to make an attempt to get our people out using capsuleer assistance. We''re concerned that more reinforcements could be on the way, and that if they arrive, we''ll lose our people for good. You need to act quickly. Your assignment is to assault the facility and return our people to us before things escalate any further.'),
(60099,'Apparently, a rival corporation is afraid of our rapid growth in the field of starship design. An “associate” of ours has informed us that a shipment of datacores heading to one of our research stations is to be intercepted by a fleet of Guristas mercenaries. What''s disturbing is that an Amarr corporation has allegedly hired the pirates to do this dirty work. If that''s true, there is a major shift in philosophy among our adversaries, both in the boardroom and in space. We need more information before we can act upon this. We want you to intercept and eliminate the Guristas threat. Find out, if you can, who is behind this. What we need is proof that our rivals are pulling their strings or that they have nothing to do with this whatsoever.'),
(60103,'A rogue drone virus has gone live at a mining colony. The machinery is malfunctioning and the problem spreading throughout the entire network. We sent a small rescue crew and it took over their systems. The crews are still alive but they''re held hostage by their own ships. Unfortunately, we can''t let that cloud our judgment. The infection must be destroyed… completely. We have reason to believe your capsuleer vessel will be able to withstand infection long enough to eradicate the problem. ---- Rogue Drones Rogue drones and wild drones are the terms used over advanced drones that mutated out of control. A few years ago some ingenious Gallente inventor had the idea of creating super-advanced drones that could think and act on their own - in essence acting in every sense like a regular space ship except being unmanned and computer controlled. First prototypes were encouraging, but then disaster struck. The drones became unruly, then unmanageable. Some of these were huge - the largest drones ever constructed, these drones were even equipped with warp drives and equipped with the latest advancements in artificial intelligence. These mother drones, as they were called, along with several lesser drones soon managed to spread out, not only within the same system as the research facility that birthed them, but also to other systems. Only later men discovered exactly how - the drones attacked and took over space ships, then used them to jump to other systems, the drones themselves safely hidden within the ship. Needless to say the super-drone research was soon abandoned by the Gallente.'),
(60104,'It appears the Gallente have been making hostile moves again in the system. They''ve been continuously launching attacks from a command vessel somewhere in a deadspace pocket. Our scouts have located the Federation admiral responsible for these raids and now we just need her taken care of. We''ve dealt with this thing before, so we''re confident that removing her from the picture will disrupt the rest of the Gallente operations in our area. The only issue is that the Navy won''t be able to mobilize against her in time – they''re the Navy after all, not a hit squad. I''ve been asked to recruit a capsuleer if possible, so we can bypass internal military procedures altogether. That''s where you come in . We need you to travel over to , enter the deadspace pocket our scouts have found, then kill the commander and her fleet. She''ll undoubtedly be back at some point even if your mission is successful. The Gallente are a persistent enemy, so after you''ve killed her, leave the body in the communication array she''s been coordinating the forces out of. That should send a message. It might even spook her into seeking reassignment elsewhere, away from our corporation''s space.'),
(60105,'I''ve got a delicate yet dangerous task that just wouldn''t suit anyone other than a capsuleer. Here''s the situation: We caught a Caldari operative trying to walk out of the University of Caille with, and I say this literally, an armful of data cores stolen from the university''s research hospital. We''ve had him locked down at a penal instillation in since then, but our more convincing interrogators have changed his mind about giving up some information. The catch is that he''s demanded to be transferred to a more "dignified" location before he offers his full cooperation. That''s where you come in. Pick up the Caldari operative and bring him back here immediately.'),
(60106,'A portion of the fleet is preparing a set of protracted war games in the next few days. There was some mix up with a circuitry order that I only just found out about. Collect the custom circuitry from the production line in Emolgranlan. The level of piracy in the area is unknown.'),
(60107,'I have a task that must be done quickly, and it requires punitive force. A new race track is being designed and built in , and it is supposed to be the grandest and most beautiful and complicated tracks yet ever to exist in all of the known sectors! A substantial quantity of money and work have gone into this track, and there are plans to hold one of the largest races ever as soon as the track is finished. However, some suspicious ships have been seen in the vicinity. They evade patrols, but we''ve received reports that they bear Gallente markings. A couple of "accidents" have already occurred while testing the track, and investigations have led to suspicion of sabotage. We think that these Gallente ships have been sabotaging this new track, probably in hopes of killing many Holders and their families when the time comes for the great inaugural race. I want you to put a stop to this nonsense before it has any further impact. Destroy those ships; it''s time we sent a message.'),
(60109,'I have just the thing you want. This one was issued from high command, specifically to be assigned to you. Recently we have been picking up signals from an old ship wreckage nearby. We send a scout to go check it out and he reported a large Serpentis presence, led by a high-ranking colonel. They seem to be looting the wreckage and creating some sort of modified Megathron battleship. If you could go and eliminate this threat, we will reward you nicely.'),
(60111,'There''s been an influx of neural boosters to our area recently, and Caldari Navy is trying to stem the flow. We normally turn a blind eye to light drug trafficking but that only seems to have encouraged the local smugglers, who are now flooding the area with cheap, more dangerous drugs. We know where they base out of, however, and have already taken the liberty of blockading their station in the Isaziwa system. What we need is a capsuleer who can go in there and check out some of the larger vessels currently in holding. You are of course cleared to engage anyone caught with illegal boosters in their cargo, although if you catch anyone be prepared for them to start shooting.'),
(60113,'A confidential informant has warned us of an impending kidnapping attempt on a young noble by a notorious Minmatar mercenary. One of my associates, who owes me a lifetime worth of favors, discovered the plot during a card game. The merc''s mouth and ego are both the size of New Eden itself. He talked openly about his plan without a second thought. We need your help in stopping him before he can carry out his plans. His staging ground is at . Find and kill him with any and all means at your disposal. He''s a crafty SOB, so expect not just a fight, but some unorthodox challenges when he realizes you''re on to him. He''s especially fond of drawing pursuers into hazardous clouds. Odds are good he''ll have some ex-Navy Minnies flying back-up. He might be a braggart, but he''s still a paranoid merc. Be careful.'),
(60140,'I''m glad you made your way here, . We had an amazing breach of security earlier today when a band of Angel Cartel agents managed to infiltrate one of our shipyards and steal some very valuable equipment from its compounds. We''ve tracked them down to a Cartel supply depot in Ysiette, where they have set up a defensive perimeter in preparation for an attack. I know this might be a difficult assignment for you, Bluddenguttz, but it''s vital that we retrieve the stolen goods from those thieving vermin. Our spies tell us that the equipment we''re looking for is located in one of their storage facilities in the depot, still in its sealed container. Don''t hesitate to destroy the structure, in order to retrieve the goods. And you can keep anything extra you find there. Good luck.'),
(60141,'I''m glad you made your way here, . We had an amazing breach of security earlier today when a band of Blood Raider agents managed to infiltrate one of our shipyards and steal some very valuable equipment from its compounds. We''ve tracked them down to a Blood Raider supply depot in Onirvura, where they have set up a defensive perimeter in preparation for an attack. I know this might be a difficult assignment for you, , but it''s vital that we retrieve the stolen goods from those blood-sucking vermin. Our spies tell us that the equipment we''re looking for is located in one of their storage facilities in the depot, still in its sealed container. Don''t hesitate to destroy the structure, in order to retrieve the goods. And you can keep anything extra you find there. Good luck.'),
(60143,'I''m glad you made your way here, . We had an amazing breach of security earlier today when a band of Serpentis agents managed to infiltrate one of our shipyards and steal some very valuable equipment from its compounds. We''ve tracked them down to a Serpentis supply depot in Wyllequet, where they have set up a defensive perimeter in preparation for an attack. I know this might be a difficult assignment for you, , but it''s vital that we retrieve the stolen goods from those thieving vermin. Our spies tell us that the equipment we''re looking for is located in one of their storage facilities in the depot, still in its sealed container. Don''t hesitate to destroy the structure, in order to retrieve the goods. And you can keep anything extra you find there. Good luck.'),
(80064,'I just discovered why that research team never arrived to pick up the goods you ferried: their labs are under siege by Guristas forces. I don''t know what the hell the Guristas think they''re going to achieve down here, but if we don''t quickly shut them down we risk them gaining a foothold. This attack was fierce and well-coordinated. They managed to overwhelm our defenses. All of our other forces are either too far away to assist or on other important missions they can''t be diverted from. You''re our best shot. I want you to save that research station from the Guristas assault.'),
(80076,'Aren''t you the lucky one? All the carnage you''ve inflicted on our enemies has caught the attention of SARO. They are the best that CONCORD has to offer, and they''re not to be balked at. This particular SARO pilot''s name is Treonis, and she''s been asking for you personally. My guess? Taking you out is her bid at a promotion. Normally, we would launch a whole campaign to remove CONCORD scum from our space, but my superiors want to see you handle this situation. If you can destroy Treonis, I''m authorized to reward you with a single run blueprint for one of our rarer ships, the Cynabal. Treonis is waiting for you by an abandoned colony in . Destroy her, and the blueprint is yours. ---- SARO Despite CONCORD''s strong association with empire space, they occasionally sponsor larger campaigns out in nullsec. These excursions are targeted at the "pirate" factions under the justification of returning the violence committed in high security space. CONCORD''s Special Affairs for Regulations & Order (SARO) is uniquely suited for these campaigns. Their training, hardware, and skill make them a threat not to be taken lightly.'),
(90000,'"The deal," as you so quaintly put it, my young friend, is this: The station manager of recently reported to us a serious lack of mono-cell batteries in their supply depot, a situation that could result in a temporary shutdown of the entire station. We need to help them out, and I''d like you to deliver the necessary goods to them. Simple enough, eh? Well, are you interested or not? I know of several others who would happily take this offer in your stead.'),
(90001,'I want these elite troops delivered to for inspection. We hired them recently from an Amarrian security firm to work as guards on our transport vessels. Standard procedure requires that they be inspected for any possible diseases or mental disorders before they''re allowed on board.'),
(90002,'For you, my friend, there''s always something. One commodity we all have a hard time living without is oxygen. One of our buyers is on a station that''s close to running out of air, so I want you to fly over to and give them a bit more.'),
(90003,'An arms dealer passing through the system just sold us a cache of weapons. I need you to take it to for me. Don''t worry, we''ve already acquired a permit for them, so you won''t have any trouble at customs.'),
(90004,'Yes, I have something for you. A group of lads from have been requested by the army to . I''ve agreed to their request, and I''d like you to carry it out. Deliver them to their destination, the faster the better.'),
(90005,'Yes, I have something for you. One of our transports flying through broke down and requires immediate repairs. We''ve agreed to send him the spare parts he needs to complete the operation, and I''d like you to deliver the goods. If you''re fast he might even make it on time, so don''t tarry!'),
(90006,'Sure, I''ve got something. I need you to run over to and drop off these electronic parts. The Chief Technical Operator there contacted me regarding the discovery of a major defect in their primary reactor, and they don''t have the parts on hand to repair it.'),
(90007,'Here at , we''re all about pleasure. I''m sure you''ve seen our adverts — "If it''s fun, it must be from ." And it just so happens that we''re opening some new clubs over in . The problem is that the talent has gotten stranded here, and has to be over to the station for the grand opening. What talent you ask? Well, I mean the dancers, ... Exotic dancing is an art form, you know, appreciated on the highest intellectual level. And we''ve got a bunch of dancers just standing around waiting for a ship to take ''em to their new home. You probably know the rest. We need a fast, reliable pilot and a ship without any major mechanical problems. That brave and resourceful pilot needs to take these dancers to their destination so that they can get bringing in the high-rollers and thus earning their wages. It''s important that this be taken care of soon, so we''re offering a substantial reward to anyone who wants to take the job. You up to it, kid?'),
(90008,'Yes, I have something for you. It''s tough to quit smoking when you''ve got a warehouse full of cigarettes within arm''s reach. Take every crate of that crap you can find in that warehouse over to and leave it there. Quickly, before I change my mind!'),
(90009,'I have just the thing you want. A spate of engine failures and system crashes at a client firm in has forced them to come to us for more coolants. We have some extras available, which I''d like you to deliver. Get it done in time, before their manager suffers a nervous breakdown, to earn your bonus.'),
(90010,'Something just came up that''s right up your alley. You have established yourself as a trustworthy client of . I have some corporate documents for you to deliver to . You have 24 hours to get this done; that should be no problem for someone as yourself, right? I assure you the reward will be well worth the effort.'),
(90011,'Yes, I have something for you. The greenhouses at need a delivery of fertile soil. Take these crates and deliver them, would you? Thanks. Have an excellent day!'),
(90012,'Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. My superiors over at are waiting for these reports. I''m swamped with work so I need you to deliver them for me. Don''t mess this up. Both our jobs are on the line here.'),
(90013,'Something just came up that''s right up your alley. Homeless people are everywhere, littering the streets. I''ve gathered up a whole bunch of them, and I want you to go and dump them at . Make it somebody else''s problem!'),
(90014,'Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. My friend is getting married. We need entertainment for his bachelor party tomorrow, but I can''t just show up with the dancers myself. Take these "performers" to for me. Be sure to get them there on time so we can start the fun!'),
(90015,'Well, you''re pretty green, by the look of you, but I''ve got no choice. You may have heard all the rumors. The entire frontier is buzzing with reports that we''re pretty much at war with the Amarrians. I can''t say either way, for sure, but I do know that all this war talk has led to some big headaches when it comes to commercial traffic and trade-route management. Passenger liners are all booked, haulers have been pre-empted by the military or by wealthy clients... god, it''s just a mess out there. Anyway, as you may have seen, the docks here at are filled to overflowing with tons of goods, and we can''t seem to find enough transport to get them to their destinations. I need to get some of this stuff out of here. Ah, here: we''ve got a shipment of vaccines that need to be delivered to in a hurry. I''m willing to provide a substantial bonus if they''re delivered right away. Regardless, the meds need to be delivered soon, though. Say the word and you can move the stuff into your cargo hold. Can you do it?'),
(90016,'We were ordered by high ranking officials in the to deliver a batch of Zemnar to the inhabitants of . Their supplies are low and they need some backup incase of a viral outbreak. |collapsed= yes'),
(90017,'needs some goods moved to in a jiffy. Are you up for the job, ?'),
(90018,'I have just the thing you want. To eliminate the depressive mood of our hangar staff, cargo bay workers, janitors and other laborers we decided to throw them a party at . I''d like you to do the honors of delivering the spiced wine to the gathering. And don''t forget, a quick delivery will get you a bonus!'),
(90019,'Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. Have you seen the price of oil around here lately? It''s absurd! Our clients are demanding more, but all we''ve got is the synthetic stuff, so take a load of it over to .'),
(90020,'Well, it''s my sister. I mean, I remembered her birthday this time, I swear. I planned out the gift, got it ordered in advance — and it was not cheap, let me tell you. I found a specialty perfume maker, and it turns out my sister likes the smells of really damn expensive things. And of course the fancy-pants perfumer has a ridiculous waiting list. But I got everything done in time! I just need you to deliver it. I''ll pay you, okay?'),
(90021,'Yes, I have something for you. The local news recently aired a story on poor immigrants in . Apparently some of the families have fallen on hard times and lack the funds to even buy the most basic necessities. A few concerned citizens in asked me to have these clothes delivered to the needy in , which they can make use of. I''d like you to make the first leg of the trip, which is to drop off the goods at . Officials at the station will take care of the rest.'),
(90022,'Well, yes. Now, I can''t say too much, but something''s come up, and there''s a great need for ground troops in a nearby system. You may have noticed all those marines hanging out in the loading bay. We''ve grabbed every available transport we can find, but there''s still a few left behind who need to be transported to . Suffice to say, their presence is of vital importance to Federation efforts, and if you''re a loyal citizen, you''ll take them to their destination. And of course there''s some extra pay in it for you. Will you help? |collapsed= yes'),
(90023,'We''ve been having some trouble with deliveries ending up at incorrect destinations. I guess these shipping companies can''t be trusted to do their job properly, so I need you to fill in for them. Take these holoreels to ; I will reward you for the effort.'),
(90024,'Excellent. As you know, it is the duty of every citizen to demonstrate his or her loyalty to the state from time to time. Though you are, at present, a small cog in the great machine of the Empire, you will find that even you have your place. We have a task for you that will help show your fitness to advance in our society and become a more significant part of that great machine. It seems that the construction works at are experiencing an unfortunate labor shortage, possibly brought on by their overly harsh personnel management methods. It is important to the Empire that we get them a shipment of elite slaves so that they do not fall any further behind schedule. Are you a loyal enough citizen to do this task and do it quickly? I will upload a bookmark to your People & Places databank; use it to locate and reach your destination.'),
(90025,'One of the mining colonies didn''t receive their supplies last week, and if we don''t do anything about it they''re going to starve. We have some extra supplies here that I want you to transport to 1DH-SX III - Moon 1 - Blood Raiders Logistic Support.'),
(90026,'Our friends in are worried their oxygen supplies won''t last until the next shipment from their supplier. They''ve requested an extra batch, and we''ve promised to deliver. You''ll find the goods in your cargo hold if you agree to this task.'),
(90027,'We just discovered a colony of people we didn''t know were there on a nearby planet. Our diplomats are planning a trip to negotiate with them on working for us in the constellation. Please transport our supply of Vitoc to KFIE-Z VIII - Moon 18 - Blood Raiders Logistic Support. They can''t go until this stuff arrives, so hurry up.'),
(90028,'Slaves at a nearby station are rebelling. They''ve managed to break their way into an armory and are holding their ground there. Please transport these small arms to the station to assist our security personnel in putting them in their place.'),
(90029,'Sure, I''ve got something. I have assets at that are in need of additional protection. We''ve hired a group of marines to take care of the problem. Go to and drop them off.'),
(90030,'For you, my friend, there''s always something. Surprisingly, people seem to enjoy visiting . I personally think the place is rather boring, but command has ordered me to take care of some high-profile tourists for the next week. Ferry these tourists over to for me, would you? That should keep them busy, at least.'),
(90031,'These are dark days for our Republic, as you know. Our enemies threaten us on all sides, and our ancient traditions are in danger of dying out. We are a race of warriors, , and only through strength do we survive in a hostile universe. Our strength is in our warriors and in their weapons. We believe that the cursed Amarrians are planning a major invasion, and we need to equip our warriors to repel their attacks on planetary environs. On the loading dock is a shipment of weapons for our 412th Regiment, currently garrisoned at . Can you get it there for them?'),
(90032,'"The deal," as you so quaintly put it, my young friend, is this: The station manager of recently reported to us a serious lack of mono-cell batteries in their supply depot, a situation that could result in a temporary shutdown of the entire station. We need to help them out, and I''d like you to deliver the necessary goods to them. Simple enough, eh? Well, are you interested or not? I know of several others who would happily take this offer in your stead.'),
