(90084,'We were ordered by high ranking officials in the to deliver a batch of Zemnar to the inhabitants of . Their supplies are low and they need some backup incase of a viral outbreak. |collapsed= yes'),
(90085,'needs some goods moved to in a jiffy. Are you up for the job, ?'),
(90086,'I have just the thing you want. To eliminate the depressive mood of our hangar staff, cargo bay workers, janitors and other laborers we decided to throw them a party at . I''d like you to do the honors of delivering the spiced wine to the gathering. And don''t forget, a quick delivery will get you a bonus!'),
(90087,'Here is a mission suited for someone of your caliber. Have you seen the price of oil around here lately? It''s absurd! Our clients are demanding more, but all we''ve got is the synthetic stuff, so take a load of it over to .'),
(90088,'Yes, I have something for you. The local news recently aired a story on poor immigrants in . Apparently some of the families have fallen on hard times and lack the funds to even buy the most basic necessities. A few concerned citizens in asked me to have these clothes delivered to the needy in , which they can make use of. I''d like you to make the first leg of the trip, which is to drop off the goods at . Officials at the station will take care of the rest.'),
(90089,'We''ve been having some trouble with deliveries ending up at incorrect destinations. I guess these shipping companies can''t be trusted to do their job properly, so I need you to fill in for them. Take these holoreels to ; I will reward you for the effort.'),
(90090,'Our friends in are worried their oxygen supplies won''t last until the next shipment from their supplier. They''ve requested an extra batch, and we''ve promised to deliver. You''ll find the goods in your cargo hold if you agree to this task.'),
(90091,'Sure, I''ve got something. I have assets at that are in need of additional protection. We''ve hired a group of marines to take care of the problem. Go to and drop them off.'),
(90092,'For you, my friend, there''s always something. Surprisingly, people seem to enjoy visiting . I personally think the place is rather boring, but command has ordered me to take care of some high-profile tourists for the next week. Ferry these tourists over to for me, would you? That should keep them busy, at least.'),
(91000,'We need your help right away! We''re calling on all ship commanders in this region. A huge asteroid has crashed into one of our stations. The station itself and most of the inhabitants are lost. This asteroid is particularly deadly in that it contains a huge quantity of Augumene, a rare and extremely toxic ore. We need someone to mine out the Augumene so rescue crews can go in there and retrieve the survivors. I''ve uploaded a bookmark to your People & Places databank; use it to find the crash site and then use a survey scanner to locate the Augumene. Mine it all and bring the ore back to me.'),
(91001,'Well, maybe, yeah. Have you ever heard of Banidine? Doesn''t matter, you have now. Anyway, my boss wants the stuff. Why? I have no idea — something to do with manufacturing cheaper parts, refrigeration units or something. I don''t know. Point is, he''s made it my job to get the ore. And now, if you''re interested, I''m makin'' it your job. There''s a few Banidine rocks out at , enough for 20,000 units, the scouts tell me. Go out there, mine it, bring it back. Should be easy enough, right?'),
(91002,'Something terrible has happened. An asteroid has collided with a research station at . There''s no official death-toll yet, but it''s expected to climb into the tens of thousands. Some of our brightest were there, working out the very technologies that would enable us to better defend our way of life from Gallente and Minmatar agressors. Now they''re all gone.... I''m sorry. I lost myself there. We''ve determined that the asteroid that collided with the station was composed of Augumene, a rare and extremely toxic ore. We need someone to mine out the Augumene safely from a starship. More than that, others may be coming for the Augumene. We can''t recover all the sensitive material from the wreckage of the station in time, and a blockade would tip our hand. The only solution is to mine out the Augumene ourselves. We want you to go out and retrieve all 3,600 units of Augumene from the site. And hurry. If we don''t get that ore, looters might follow its signal and stumble on what''s left of our base.'),
(91003,'To be part of the future you need to help build it first. That''s what I''m asking you to do. There''s a rare ore called Mercium, similar to Omber, but it''s much more difficult to reprocess. Current methods render the ore unusable. It''s maddening to no end. I think I might have solved the problem, though. I can''t tell you my whole theory, but it''s a variant on the standard electrolysis method used by planetside miners. All I need is some Mercium to try it on. There''s a rich deposit of Mercium in this system. Bring me 1,800 units and we might both end up rich.'),
(91004,'Damnation, they''re sending them out younger and younger. Are you sure you''re old enough to fly a starship? Oh, well, we have to play the hand we''re dealt, and if you''re the best I can get, I suppose you''ll do. We''ll start simple, youngster. Banidine is normally all but worthless, so real miners don''t usually bother with the stuff. Still, I''ve found a buyer who''s willing to take whatever we can mine. So, get me 20,000 units of Banidine and I''ll make it worth your while. It should be easy, even for a pup like you, but it will show me that you''re serious. There''s an asteroid field near here that''s lousy with the stuff – I''ve bookmarked it for you. Get back as soon as you can and I''ll arrange a little bonus.'),
(91005,'We recently found a number of new mining fields in adjacent systems, and the usual assortment of pirate trash has come out of the woodwork to exploit it. We''ll need them mined soon because even those thieving bastards have friends in places high enough to put the legal status of these sites in doubt. For some reason they''ve taken an interest even in Banidine, too, and we''ll need to find out why; all my workers are busy with the more profitable fields, but I''m not taking any chances. I''m uploading a bookmark to your People & Places databank; it shows the location of a Banidine mining operation. I need you to head out there and mine all the Banidine — should be 18,000 units, my foreman tells me. Once we''ve made an undisputed claim, we''re free to mine there again without interference, and I''ll provide you with a little something for your trouble.'),
(91006,'We''ve found a conglomeration of Augumene asteroids nearby. The ore''s not much good to anyone due to the exorbitant cost of reprocessing, of course, but a couple of our scientists are interested in doing some research on such a rare substance. In any case, hopefully you''ve been around the block enough times that you can find the ore and bring it in.'),
(91007,'Oh, right. I was thinking I''d already sent you a com-chat about this. Heh. Sorry. One of our sources obtained information on the whereabouts of a significant deposit of Mercium ore. It would be disastrous for our cause if this Mercium were to fall into Amarrian or Caldari hands. Unfortunately, we''re certain that they already know about it, so as I said, we must work quickly. Remember, they want that Mercium, so that means we need it more. Get it? You do whatever you have to to get this done quickly, alright?'),
(91008,'Well, we''ve got a bit of a weird one here. We''ve found an old mining post in . But, the thing is, we can''t find who used to own it: There are no records of its being built or even existing. It''s simply empty. No sign of anyone left there, dead or otherwise. Our initial investigation found extensive fire damage, gas leaks — you name it, it went wrong. Lots of explosive damage, though we can''t tell if that was accidental or intentional. And some marks... well, we just don''t know what could do that to metal. It''s damn creepy, that''s for sure. Anyway, near as we can tell, the miners were working on a large Lyavite deposit. They didn''t finish, because there''s still about 5,000 units of it at the site. Now, I know Lyavite isn''t the most popular rock, but nobody just leaves that much ore lying around. And besides, the brains at the lab figure they can use the stuff for some of their research, so this opportunity is too good to pass up. That''s where you come in. Warp in, mine the Lyavite, and warp out. It''s that easy.'),
(91009,'Chemical warfare may not be as flashy as space lasers or doomsday weapons, but it just might decide the outcome of this war we''re in. After all, what''s the value of taking over territory if all your planets are uninhabitable? Of course, our foes have found counters to most of the known chemical agents. So the key to victory will be new compounds. That''s why I want you to acquire a big bunch of Augumene for us. The stuff is insanely toxic, hence its absence on the market. But in this case, its very toxicity is what we want to harness.'),
(91010,'You ever try mining with drones? Useful little guys, huh? Yeah, well, to a point… Turns out someone got the bright idea that if mining drones mine more ore, bigger drones would mine even more ore. This guy''s team slapped some mining drone''s AI into non-regulation heavy combat units and threw some mining lasers on. He even hacked the firmware so that the mining brains could control the weaponry, making some sort of self-sufficient mining machines. But of course the genius didn''t test the things properly before sending them out to to mine Mercium. And of course now he''s made himself scarce. You can probably guess what happened. Now there''s a bunch of haywire drones zipping about this rare mineral that we want — our guys in the lab need it for research, I guess. The drones aren''t even mining the rock, last I heard, but they have tried to bore through any ship we send out there.... It''s getting ridiculous. If you can, get out to , neutralize the drones, and bring back all the Mercium; we''ll pay you well for your efforts.'),
(91011,'wants a massive shipment of Augumene right away, so we need you to get out there and bring some back. They seem to think they might be able to find some use for the stuff for chemical warfare, I guess? But that''s just between you and me, right? Anyway, I''ve been looking for a miner who''s experienced enough, with the right kind of ship, and maybe you fit the bill. Time is critical on this one. There''s a big bonus for you if you can bring it in fast enough. Seriously, we need a mountain of this stuff, so get on it. I''ve uploaded the location to your People & Places databank.'),
(91012,'A recent survey scan of reveals a big deposit of Banidine ore. We were content to leave it alone at first, but then we saw swarms of drones in the area. They seem to be making their way through the asteroid fields there in a hurry. They haven''t stumbled on the Banidine yet, but it''s only a matter of time. We want you to get to the ore before they do. I won''t lie to you; it''s going to be close. You may even have to fight a few of them off, so be careful.'),
(91013,'Yes, I think you are. Listen, our miners have just reported a bunch of rogue drones in the system. Between them and the damned ore thieves, I''m almost ready to give up. They''re worse than Gallentean greenroaches – if we don''t show them that they''re not welcome here, we''ll be up to our eyeballs. And I can''t send my guys out there if I know they might be in danger. No, we need a capsuleer on this job, someone capable of defending a ship and mining at the same time. I''ve bookmarked a mining site for you. Go on out there and, if you see any drones, take ''em out. Be caref— well, I don''t need to tell an experienced starship captain like you. You know the risks. Then mine whatever Banidine you find out there so I can find out what the damn things are so interested in.'),
(91014,'I''ve just discovered a sizable deposit of Pithix out by an old mining station. The station''s been abandoned for a while now, but there are still working sensors in the area; that''s how we picked up on the Pithix. Problem is, the transmission''s hardly secure. I need you to get out there and bring me back that rock before someone else cleans the place out. So, are you game?'),
(91015,'I''ve been having a spot of bother filling an order, . It''s starting to affect my usually sunny disposition. I''m hoping you can clear this off my docket, and bring the smile back to my face. My client requires hydrogen isotopes to run her control tower, and she''s getting a little snippy about the time it''s taking me to provide it. She''s even sent along a few assassins to vent her displeasure. No patience, that woman. , I need you to procure 10 units of a very particular ice-- Azure Ice, I believe, is what you''re looking for on your scanner; I can extract the hydrogen myself. I''ve lost a few good ships and a few incompetent pilots in the ice fields trying to fill this order, and I really need you to live up to your reputation, -- within the next 24 hours. Can I count on you, ?'),
(91016,'Look, I hear there''s some Green Arisite that a bunch of people are looking to get their hands on. Now, I don''t know why they want it, but if they want it, I want it. You may have to hunt for it a bit; I hear the belt''s got a lot of big broken-up old asteroids floating around. Might be a little creepy, but it shouldn''t do you any harm, and I want that damn rock! Go get it before those other bastards get their grubby hands on it!'),
(91017,'Alright! You ever been out to some of those backwater colonies? You know the ones I mean. Barren wastelands of rocks and dust where some nut got the bright idea to try to build the agricultural community of tomorrow? Kind of place where the main export is despair? That kind of place? Well, so happens I know of one that''s just starting up. Poor bastards need some fuel. They''re willing to pay good money, too. Now, I could sell them the good stuff, but seriously, these jokers wouldn''t know good ice if it fell out of the sky and crushed their pet furrier. There''s a field of Azure Ice at Hageken. It''s not as good as Blue Ice, but the colonists won''t know the difference. Bring me back about, oh, 20 blocks of it. I''ll sell it to the colony goobers and cut you in. Sound good? You will need an Ice Harvester module to complete this mission. Also, be aware that this amount of raw Azure Ice may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space.'),
(91018,'It''s the sound of war! It''s been too long since the blaring of military marches has been heard, the stockpiling of weapons undertaken, the murderous idealism of a young generation inveigled. And to me it all seems like the clinking of ISK. War is one of the biggest boons to business you could hope for. It''s a hungry giant that will eat anything you can throw at it. And the thing is, if you don''t feed it, it will just eat you…. But if you feed it well? Oh, the rewards. Public recognition, sure, but the contracts, the contracts, ! That''s where the real ISK is. And we''re going to get those contracts. Oh, yes. But first we need minerals. Right now, it seems the giant on our doorstep wants Oeryl, and we''re going to give it to him. There''s a deposit out at . Bring back all 5,600 units of the stuff and I''ll make sure you get your share of the reward.'),
(91019,'has an unusual request for the right miner. We need a big shipment of Geodite crystals for a client of ours, some gemology lab. Maybe you''ve heard of Geodite, but if not, it''d be no surprise — the stuff''s pretty much worthless. But these gemologists figure they might be able to get some decent stones out of it and make a bit of profit that way. Whatever. They want to pay for it, so it''s all good by me. And you''ll get your cut, don''t worry. Anyway, if you''re interested, I''ll send the coordinates over to your ship''s NeoCom — the field''s in this system.'),
(91020,'Right away. But look, this one''s a little weird. Just a heads up. There''s this guy who''s making these really, truly gigantic ice sculptures — some kinda artsy shit, I don''t know. I said, buddy, that much ice, it''s gonna melt before you can finish carving it, or it''s gonna break under its own weight. He says he knows that, says that''s why he''s gonna build it in space! Crazy… Anyway, he''s got the money, so what am I gonna say but "how much and how fast?" So, can you get 20 units of Crystalline Icicles over here ASAP? I got a location for you. {{Co|red|You will need an Ice Harvester module to complete this mission. Also, be aware that this amount of raw Crystalline Icicles ore may require multiple trips unless you have a large amount of cargo space'),
(91021,'Well, we''ve located some asteroids that contain substantial amounts of Polygypsum. It''s a comparatively rare mineral, and almost completely unknown in this system. Our guys want to have a look at the stuff and see if they can figure out some way to make use of it; however, we don''t have anyone who wants to deal with the stuff. So guess who I thought of first? You''ll need to grab all 2,800 units of the stuff and get it back here. So what do you think? Are you in?'),
(91022,'I do. And it''s going to be a big haul. Demand for minerals is skyrocketing. All the big empires are stockpiling for the coming fight. Oh, come on, you''ve seen the signs! Ships, rockets, drones, fortifications — all these things take material. The skirmishes out in 0.0 aren''t lessening the demand any, either. Which is good for us. More demand means more profit. To fill that demand, we''re having to turn to some unorthodox ores. Green Arisite, for instance. I know of a large field that''s full of the stuff. If you can get it for me, I''ll make sure you''re reimbursed. We just may be able to make some use of it, with the right tech. Who knows?')
